  <para style="h">Akpa Ñwed Kọrint</para>
  <para style="toc1">Akpa Ñwed Kọrint</para>
  <para style="toc2">Akpa Ñwed Kọrint</para>
  <para style="toc3">1Kọr</para>
  <para style="mt1">Akpa Ñwed Kọrint</para>
  <chapter number="1" style="c" sid="1CO 1" />
  <para style="po">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="1CO 1:1" />Ami Pọọl, e-ekekoodo nọ adido abọsịd Krais Yisọs ato ke uduak Abasi ye ayịneka ñnyịn ke Krais Sostenes, <verse eid="1CO 1:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="1CO 1:2" />inọọ ñwed ami esọk ufọkabasi ke Kọrint, ye mbon e-enamma esana ke Krais Yisọs, e-enyʌññọ ekoot nọ edido mme ndisana mbon amọ ye afịd awo ke afịd itie e-ekoodo anyịñ Abọọñ ñnyịn Yisọs Krais, Abọọñ ammọ ye ake ñnyịn. <verse eid="1CO 1:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="1CO 1:3" />Mfọn ye emem a-atooho Abasi Ete ñnyịn ye Abọọñ Yisọs Krais akpekap ado udeeme ndufo.<verse eid="1CO 1:3" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Ekọọm</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="1CO 1:4" />Ami mmekọọm Abasi afịd ini inọ ndufo ato ke mfọn a-Abasi inọọhọ ndufo ato ke Krais Yisọs. <verse eid="1CO 1:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="1CO 1:5" />Sia ato ke anye ndufo e-emọinyọ ke afịd usʌñ ke afịd aditañ ikọ ye ke afịd ifiọk, <verse eid="1CO 1:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="1CO 1:6" />Abasi anyʌñ asọọñọ ntiense ñnyịn ke abaña Krais ke idem ndufo. <verse eid="1CO 1:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="1CO 1:7" />Ke ntoro, ndufo inanake enọ Adisana Sịbidịd ndomokeed ke ini ndufo esʌkkọ ebet adiyaara Abọọñ ñnyịn Yisọs Krais. <verse eid="1CO 1:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="1CO 1:8" />Anye ayaanyʌñ isọọñọ ndufo idem tutu asịm utịd nọ ato do ndufo ediinana ndo ke usen Abọọñ ñnyịn Yisọs Krais. <verse eid="1CO 1:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="1CO 1:9" />Abasi a-akikoodo ndufo asịn ke ewuana ye Ayịn amọ Yisọs Krais Abọọñ ñnyịn ado anam akpanikọ.<verse eid="1CO 1:9" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Ubakka Nda ke Ufọọd mme Adaiwuod ke Ufọkabasi</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="1CO 1:10" />Ami mmedat anyịñ Abọọñ ñnyịn Yisọs Krais ikpe ndufo ubọk, nditọeka<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1:10 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Ke usem Greek adelfọi awuọñọke </char><char style="fq" closed="false">nditọeka </char><char style="fqa" closed="false">awodeen ye awonwaan </char><char style="ft" closed="false">anyʌñ ada anọ mbon e-enịmme Krais ke akpanikọ, edoho ideen ye ibaan ke atu ubon Abasi; se ñko ke Rom 17:11 ye 26; ke Rom 2:1; Rom 3:1, Rom 4:6; Rom 6:8; Rom 7:24, 29; Rom 10:1; Rom 11:33; Rom 12:1; Rom 14:6, 20, 26, 39; Rom 15:1. 6, 50, 58; Rom 16:15, 20</char></note> ke Krais, nte yak afịd ndufo enyịmme ye emọ-emọ ke se ndufo etañ ye se enam, mbaak ubakka adiba ke atu ndufo, ado nọ ato do ndufo ediana keed ke esịd ye ke akikere. <verse eid="1CO 1:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="1CO 1:11" />Nditọeka ke Krais, usʌk awo ke ufọk Klọ, endọkkọ miin ke utọk aba ke ufọọd ndufo. <verse eid="1CO 1:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="1CO 1:12" />Se ami ntañ mbaña ado ke awo keed abo, “Ami ñkeene Pọọl; awo mfen ate, Ami ñkeene Apọlọs; awo mfen ate, Ami ñkeene Kefas; ñnwen ate, Ami ñkeene Krais.”<verse eid="1CO 1:12" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="1CO 1:13" />Ado nte ebabakka Krais? Ado nte ekekọñ Pọọl ke krọs inọọ ndufo? Ado nte ekiduọk ndufo mmọọñ esịn ke anyịñ Pọọl? <verse eid="1CO 1:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="1CO 1:14" />Ami mmekọọm Abasi ke ñkiduọkkọ awo ndufo ndomokeed mmọọñ ke imiibọhọke Krispus ye Kayọs, <verse eid="1CO 1:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="1CO 1:15" />mbaak awo ndomokeed adibo ke ekiduọk ndufo mmọọñ ke anyịñ mmi. <verse eid="1CO 1:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="1CO 1:16" />(Ii, ami mmaanyʌñ nduọk mbon ufọk Stefanas mmọọñ, ndin ke aboiyoke ado, ntoiyoke me mmaaduọk awo mfen mmọọñ.) <verse eid="1CO 1:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="1CO 1:17" />Sia Krais ikindọññọ miin ibo ndiduọk mmọọñ ado akendọñ abo ndikwọrọ eti etob, itooho ke akpọsọñ aniọñ ye ndọọn, mbaak krọs Krais adinana adudu amọ.<verse eid="1CO 1:17" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Krais e-Ekekọññọ ke Krọs Ado Aniọñ ye Adudu Abasi</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="1CO 1:18" />Etob krọs ibaaha ufọn inọ mbon nsobo, ado ado adudu Abasi inọ ñnyịn mbon e-emaekenyaaña. <verse eid="1CO 1:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="1CO 1:19" />Sia e-ewet ete:</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="1CO 1:19">“Ami ñyaasobo aniọñ mbon aniọñ;</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="1CO 1:19">ñyaatịmede mbufiọk mbon mbufiọk.”<verse eid="1CO 1:19" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="1CO 1:20" />Mmọ awo aniọñ? Mmọ akpeeb mbed? Mmọ ataifiọk ayio mfịn? Nte Abasi inamma nọ aniọñ ederimbod ami akappa ado ndisịme? <verse eid="1CO 1:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="1CO 1:21" />Sia adooho ke ifiọk Abasi, ederimbod ke ifiọk ammọ ikidiọọñọke anye, Abasi amaakop inemesịd ato ke ndisịme e-ekekwọrọke enyaaña mbon se inịm ke akpanikọ. <verse eid="1CO 1:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="1CO 1:22" />Mme Yuu eyem idiọọñọ, mbon Greek eyem aniọñ, <verse eid="1CO 1:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="1CO 1:23" />ado ñnyịn ikwọrọ Krais e-ekekọññọ ke krọs, a-adooho ñkpọ ubiọọñọ anọ mme Yuu, anyʌñ ado ndisịme anọ mme Gentile, <verse eid="1CO 1:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="1CO 1:24" />ado mbon a-Abasi akoodo, mme Yuu ye mme Greek, Krais ado adudu Abasi ye aniọñ Abasi. <verse eid="1CO 1:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="1CO 1:25" />Sia Abasi ke ndisịme amọ a-adiọọñọ ñkpọ akan awo aniọñ; mmemidem Abasi anyʌñ asọñ adudu akan adudu awo.<verse eid="1CO 1:25" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" sid="1CO 1:26" />Nditọeka ke Krais, ikere ibaña se ndufo ekedo mbemiso ekikoot ndufo. Uwak ndufo ikidooho mbon akpọsọñ aniọñ ke udomo ñkpọ awo; uwak ndufo ikidooho mme awuọiso awo; uwak ndufo ñko ikitooho ufọk ubọọñ imana. <verse eid="1CO 1:26" /><verse number="27" style="v" sid="1CO 1:27" />Ado Abasi amaamek mme ndisịme ñkpọ ederimbod nọ ato do asịn mbon aniọñ ke abuud; Abasi amek mmem-mmem ñkpọ ederimbod nọ ato do abuud amʌm awo uko. <verse eid="1CO 1:27" /><verse number="28" style="v" sid="1CO 1:28" />Abasi amaamek mme ñkpọ e-ebaaha ke usʌhọde itie ke ederimbod ye mme ñkpọ e-esịnne ke ndek, ye mme ñkpọ se imiibaaha, nọ ebiat mme ñkpọ se iba, <verse eid="1CO 1:28" /><verse number="29" style="v" sid="1CO 1:29" />mbaak awo ndomokeed adiduaak inua ke iso Abasi. <verse eid="1CO 1:29" /><verse number="30" style="v" sid="1CO 1:30" />Ke ntak amọ ke ndufo eba ke Krais Yisọs, a-amaakekappa ado aniọñ a-atooho Abasi inọ ñnyịn, a-adooho, adinenido, adisana ido ye ufak ñnyịn. <verse eid="1CO 1:30" /><verse number="31" style="v" sid="1CO 1:31" />Ke ntoro, nte naña ewet: “Yak awo a-aduaha inua aduaak ke Abọọñ.”<verse eid="1CO 1:31" /></para>
  <chapter eid="1CO 1" />
  <chapter number="2" style="c" sid="1CO 2" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="1CO 2:1" />Naña akeba adoodo ye ami, nditọeka mmi ke Krais. Ke ini ami ñkediighe ibịne ndufo, ñkidiighe ye akpọsọñ ndọọn ikọ me aniọñ a-atooho awo ke ini ñketañña ikọ ntiense inọọ ndufo mbaña Abasi.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">2:1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Usʌk mme ikpañwed ewet </char><char style="fq" closed="false">ñketañña </char><char style="fqa" closed="false">ntọtʌñọ </char></note> <verse eid="1CO 2:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="1CO 2:2" />Sia ami mmaabiide aditre adidiọọñọ ñkpọ ndomokeed ke ini ñkebaaha ye ndufo ke amaaboiyo Yisọs Krais e-ekekọññọ ke krọs. <verse eid="1CO 2:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="1CO 2:3" />Ami ñkedi ibịne ndufo ke mmemidem ye akpọsọñ ndịk ye ñnyeñidem. <verse eid="1CO 2:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="1CO 2:4" />Etob mmi ye ukwọrọikọ mmi ikisañake ye aniọñ ye ikọ ndukpek, ado akeben adudu Sịbidịd anam uwọdñkpọ, <verse eid="1CO 2:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="1CO 2:5" />mbaak mbuọdidem ndufo adikeene ifiọk awo, ado akeene adudu Abasi.<verse eid="1CO 2:5" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Sịbidịd Ayaara Aniọñ Abasi</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="1CO 2:6" />Kpayeado, imisʌk ineme ikọ aniọñ inọ mme adiọọñọidem awo, ado idooho aniọñ ayio mfịn me ake mme andikara ayio mfịn, e-ediwuọñọ ikpu-ikpu. <verse eid="1CO 2:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="1CO 2:7" />Iyoo, ñnyịn itañ ikọ ibaña ndedịbe aniọñ ake Abasi, aniọñ e-emaekedịp, ake Abasi akebeeñeke anịm anọ ubọọñ ñnyịn ke editọọñọ mbemiso ntọọñọ ederimbod. <verse eid="1CO 2:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="1CO 2:8" />Ikinwañake mme andikara ayio ami ndomokeed sia akpedo amaanwaña ammọ, ammọ ikpikikọññọ Abọọñ ubọọñ ke krọs. <verse eid="1CO 2:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="1CO 2:9" />Kpayeado, naña ewet:</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="1CO 2:9">“Se anyen ndomokeed imiikịtte,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="1CO 2:9">se utọñ ndomokeed imiikoppo,</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="1CO 2:9">ye se esịd awo ndomokeed imiikereke,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="1CO 2:9">mme ñkpọ se Abasi abeeñe anịm anọ mbon se ima anye.”<verse eid="1CO 2:9" /></para>
  <para style="m">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="1CO 2:10" />Mme ñkpọ ami ado se Abasi ayaara iwọt ñnyịn ke Sịbidịd amọ.</para>
  <para style="p" vid="1CO 2:10">Sịbidịd aduunọ afịd ñkpọ, kpa ye ntəño-ntəño ñkpọ Abasi. <verse eid="1CO 2:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="1CO 2:11" />Anie ke atu ndufo adiọọñọ akikere esịd awo ke mmiibọhọke sịbidịd esịd mbon ado? Ke ukem usʌñ ado awo ndomokeed idiọọñọke akikere Abasi ke miibọhọke Sịbidịd Abasi. <verse eid="1CO 2:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="1CO 2:12" />Ñnyịn ibọọhọ sịbidịd ake ederimbod ado ibọ Sịbidịd a-atooho Abasi nọ ato do anekke inwaña ñnyịn se Abasi inọ ñnyịn ke ntadubọk. <verse eid="1CO 2:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="1CO 2:13" />Se ñnyịn itañ ado ami, idooho ikọ se ifiọk awo ikpeep ñnyịn, ado ke ikọ ake Sịbidịd akpeebe, atañ abaña akpanikọ ake Sịbidịd ato ke ikọ Sịbidịd. <verse eid="1CO 2:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="1CO 2:14" />Awo abʌkidem i-imiinieghe Sịbidịd ibọọhọ ñkpọ a-atooho Sịbidịd Abasi sia atie anye ndisịme-ndisịme, ñko ikanna inwaña anye sia ediọọñọ mme ñkpọ ami eto Sịbidịd. <verse eid="1CO 2:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="1CO 2:15" />Awo a-anieghe Sịbidịd akeme inọ ubiideikpe mbaña afịd ñkpọ, ado anye ke idem amọ ibaaha ke idak ubiideikpe awo ndomokeed. <verse eid="1CO 2:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="1CO 2:16" />Sia,</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="1CO 2:16">“Anie awo adiọọñọ akikere Abọọñ</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="1CO 2:16">nọ ato do anye akpeep Abasi ñkpọ?”</para>
  <para style="m" vid="1CO 2:16">Ado ñnyịn iminie akikere Krais.<verse eid="1CO 2:16" /></para>
  <chapter eid="1CO 2" />
  <chapter number="3" style="c" sid="1CO 3" />
  <para style="s1">Ufọkabasi ye mme Adaiwuod</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="1CO 3:1" />Nditọeka ke Krais, ami ñdikanna mbo ke ndufo edo mbon eduuho uwem ke Sịbidịd, sia ndufo edo mbon abʌkidem, mme ataa ntəkayịn ke Krais. <verse eid="1CO 3:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="1CO 3:2" />Ami ñkinọ ndufo mmọọñeba, ñkinọọhọ ataa ndidia, sia ndufo ikibeeñeke idem adidia ataa ndidia. Ke akpanikọ, ndufo isʌkkọ ibebeeñe idem. <verse eid="1CO 3:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="1CO 3:3" />Ndufo esʌk edo mbon ederimbod. Nte ufịb ye utọk ebaaha ke ufọọd ndufo inamma ndufo edo mbon ederimbod? Nte ndufo inamma ñkpọ nte mme ñkaña awo? <verse eid="1CO 3:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="1CO 3:4" />Ke ini awo keed abooho, “Ami ñkeene Pọọl,” awo mfen ate, “Ami ñkeene Apọlọs,” nte ndufo idoññoke kpa ñkaña awo?<verse eid="1CO 3:4" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="1CO 3:5" />Nsoo ke Apọlọs ado? Nsoo ñko ke Pọọl ado? Mbon ami edoñño mme isʌñutom a-atooho ke ammọ ndufo ekenịm Krais ke akpanikọ, kpa nte Abọọñ anọọhọ awo keedekeed ubiọñutom amọ. <verse eid="1CO 3:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="1CO 3:6" />Ami ñketọ ñkpasi, Apọlọs aduọk mmọọñ, ado Abasi ado andinam nọ akọt. <verse eid="1CO 3:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="1CO 3:7" />Ke ntak ado, anditọ ye andiduọk mmọọñ idooho ñkpọ ndomokeed, Abasi ikpọọñ ado andinam ñkpọ akọt. <verse eid="1CO 3:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="1CO 3:8" />Anditọ ye andiduọk mmọọñ enie utom keed, eyaenyʌñ enọ ammọ keedekeed utịb a-akemme ye ubọkutom ammọ. <verse eid="1CO 3:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="1CO 3:9" />Sia ñnyịn idoñño mme anam utom Abasi; ndufo edoñño inwañ Abasi, ufọk Abasi.<verse eid="1CO 3:9" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="1CO 3:10" />Ke mfọn A-Abasi annọọhọ miin, ami mmaasịn itiad idakisọñ nte ata abọbufọk ndin awo mfen adibọp. Ado yak awo keedekeed atịñ anyen naña anye abọp. <verse eid="1CO 3:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="1CO 3:11" />Sia awo ndomokeed ikemeke isịn itiad idakisọñ mfen ikan se emaekesesịn, a-adooho Yisọs Krais. <verse eid="1CO 3:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="1CO 3:12" />Adieke awo akamake kold, me silfa me nsọñudua itiad, me eto, me mbid, me ndak abọp adot ke itiad idakisọñ ami, <verse eid="1CO 3:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="1CO 3:13" />utom amọ ayaawuọ ada, sia usiere ayaayaara ubọkutom. Eyaeyaara ke ikañ, ndin ikañ ayaadomo ubọkutom awo keedekeed. <verse eid="1CO 3:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="1CO 3:14" />Ñkpọ se anye abọp akpesọñ ada, andibọp ayaabọ utịb. <verse eid="1CO 3:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="1CO 3:15" />Ado ikañ akpeta, ayaatak anye; anye ke idem amọ ayaabọkkọ, ado kpa nte awo a-abọkkọke awuọ ke edemeikañ.<verse eid="1CO 3:15" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="1CO 3:16" />Nte ndufo idiọọñọke ke ndufo ke idem ndufo edo tembịd Abasi ndin ke Sịbidịd Abasi mmọdo adʌñ ke idem ndufo? <verse eid="1CO 3:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="1CO 3:17" />Awo akeedodo a-asoboke tembịd Abasi, Abasi ayaasobo awo ado; sia tembịd Abasi ado adisana, ndin afịd ndufo edo tembịd ado.<verse eid="1CO 3:17" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="1CO 3:18" />Ikiibiaña idem ndufo. Awo ndufo ndomokeed akpekere ke iminie aniọñ ayio idahami, ana anye akappa ado akọi nọ ato do anye anie aniọñ. <verse eid="1CO 3:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="1CO 3:19" />Sia aniọñ ederimbod ami ado ndisịme ke iso Abasi. Kpa naña ewet: “Anye amʌm mbon aniọñ ke ñkara ammọ.” <verse eid="1CO 3:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="1CO 3:20" />Emaana ebo, “Abọọñ adiọọñọ ke akikere awo aniọñ ado ikpu-ikpu.” <verse eid="1CO 3:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="1CO 3:21" />Ke ntoro, yak awo akuukpọọ inua aba abaña mme ñkaña awo e-edooho mme adadusʌñ! Afịdñkpọ edo ake ndufo, <verse eid="1CO 3:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="1CO 3:22" />me Pọọl, me Apọlọs, me Kefas,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">3:22 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Kefas ado Pita</char></note> me ederimbod, me uwem, me ñkpa, me ayio mfịn, me ini iso, afịd inie ndufo, <verse eid="1CO 3:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="1CO 3:23" />ndin ndufo edo ake Krais, ndin Krais ado ake Abasi.<verse eid="1CO 3:23" /></para>
  <chapter eid="1CO 3" />
  <chapter number="4" style="c" sid="1CO 4" />
  <para style="s1">Eduuwem mme Nti Abọsịd</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="1CO 4:1" />Ke ntoro, akpena ndufo idat ñnyịn nte mme nditọufọk Krais ye mbon e-enọọhọ adudu ete ediọọñọ mme ndedịbe ñkpọ Abasi. <verse eid="1CO 4:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="1CO 4:2" />Ndin ana mbon e-eyaaha akpan utom esịn ke ubọk enam akpanikọ. <verse eid="1CO 4:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="1CO 4:3" />Ami ñkereke me ndufo me esob awo keed akeedodo ebiere ikpe ennọ miin; ke akpanikọ ami ke idem mmi mbiereke ikpe nnọ idem mmi. <verse eid="1CO 4:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="1CO 4:4" />Esịd mmi ana inwañ-inwañ, ado ado inamma nọ ikpe antoppo miin. Abọọñ ado abiideikpe mmi. <verse eid="1CO 4:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="1CO 4:5" />Ke ntak ado, kuubiere ikpe ubaña ñkpọ ndomokeed mbemiso ini e-ekenịmme akem; bet tutu Abọọñ adi. Anye ayaadiyaara anwa-anwa se idịbe ke ekịm anyʌñ ayaara akikere esịd mme awo. Ini ado amaakem, awo keedekeed ayaabọ itooro ato Abasi.<verse eid="1CO 4:5" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="1CO 4:6" />Idahami, nditọeka ke Krais, mmeben mme ñkpọ ami nnam udomoñkpọ ke idem mmi ye Apọlọs ke ufọn ndufo, nọ ato do ndufo ekpeep ito ñnyịn se ikọ ami awuọñọ: “Kuubọhọ adaña ñkpọ se ekewet.” Ke ntoro, ndufo idiiwọttọ idem ibaña adido andikeene awo ñnyịn keed me awo mfen. <verse eid="1CO 4:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="1CO 4:7" />Sia anie anam nọ afo akpəho ye awo mfen? Nsoo ke anie a-afo umuukubọọhọbọ? Ndin adieke adooho akebọọbọ, ntak akpọọhọ inua nte ñkpọ a-afo umuukubọọhọbọ-ọ?<verse eid="1CO 4:7" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="1CO 4:8" />Ñkọ ndufo emenie afịd se eyeyem! Ñkọ ndufo emekappa emọmọinyọ! Ndufo emetọọñọ adido mme andikaara, ndin ndufo ikarake ye ñnyịn! Ubaha nte adooho ke ndufo emaetọtọọñọ edo mme andikaara nọ ato do ñnyịn ñko ikeene ndufo ikaara! <verse eid="1CO 4:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="1CO 4:9" />Sia antie miin nte Abasi i-iben ñnyịn mme abọsịd anịm ke edem udịm, nte mbon e-ebiereke ikpe ñkpa ebo ewot ke anwa. Inịm ñnyịn nte ñkpọ ñyọọ enọ afịd ederimbod, enọ mme enyere enyʌñ ye mme awo ñko. <verse eid="1CO 4:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="1CO 4:10" />Ñnyịn idoñño ndisịme inọ Krais, ado ndufo emenekke enie aniọñ ke Krais! Ñnyịn imikop mmemidem, ado ndufo emekop uko! Ndufo emebọ ukpono, ado ñnyịn imibọ asuenne! <verse eid="1CO 4:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="1CO 4:11" />Tutu asịm idahami, ñnyịn imikop abiọọñ ye nsaditọñ, ñnyịn isịne ntaaha afọñ, ikama ñnyịn ke ukuud, ñnyịn inieghe itie idʌñ. <verse eid="1CO 4:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="1CO 4:12" />Ñnyịn iminam akpọsọñ utom ke idem ñnyịn. Ke ini isueñesueñ ñnyịn, ñnyịn idọọdiọñ; ke ini ekọbọkekọbọ ñnyịn, ñnyịn iyọọyọ; <verse eid="1CO 4:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="1CO 4:13" />ke ini etañña abʌd-abʌd ikọ idian ñnyịn, ñnyịn ibọọrọ ke ifuuro-ifuuro usʌñ. Tutu asịm ini ami, ñnyịn imikappa ido nseseppe ñkpọ a-mbon ederimbod miiyemme aba.<verse eid="1CO 4:13" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Ebeeñe ye Ndʌdutọñ Pọọl</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="1CO 4:14" />Ami ñwette ñkpọ ami mbo abuud imʌm ndufo, ado ñwet adidʌt ndufo utọñ nte mme ndima nditọ mmi. <verse eid="1CO 4:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="1CO 4:15" />Akpekọm ndufo ekenie andikpeme tọsịn duob ke Krais, ndufo inieghe mme uwak ete, sia ke Krais Yisọs ami mmaakappa ndo ete ndufo ato ke eti etob. <verse eid="1CO 4:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="1CO 4:16" />Ke ntoro, ami mmikpeiye ndufo nte yak eñkpebe miin. <verse eid="1CO 4:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="1CO 4:17" />Ntak ado anam ami ndọñ Timoti inọ ndufo, adima ayịn mmi a-anamma akpanikọ ke Abọọñ, nte ibịne ndufo. Anye ayaitoiyo ndufo eduuwem mmi ke Krais Yisọs, a-asañake akekem ke se ami ñkpeep ke afịd itie ke afịd ufọkabasi.<verse eid="1CO 4:17" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="1CO 4:18" />Usʌk ndufo emedikokko idem, nte ñkpọ e-ebooho ke ami ndiidiighe ibịne ndufo. <verse eid="1CO 4:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="1CO 4:19" />Ado ke mfọn Abasi, ami ñyaasọsọp ndisoobo ye ndufo, ndin ami ñyaaduuñọ ndiọọñọ se mbon ñkokkoidem ami etaañ ye utọ adudu se ammọ enieghe. <verse eid="1CO 4:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="1CO 4:20" />Sia abioubọọñ Abasi idooho akpọsọñ utañ ikọ, ado ado adudu. <verse eid="1CO 4:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="1CO 4:21" />Nsoo ke ndufo ekpema? Ekpema ndi ye ikpa ntʌnọ me ke ima ye ifuuro-ifuuro sịbidịd?<verse eid="1CO 4:21" /></para>
  <chapter eid="1CO 4" />
  <chapter number="5" style="c" sid="1CO 5" />
  <para style="s1">Usappa Emọ-emọ ke Ubon</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="1CO 5:1" />E-etañ ennọ ke use ye efịbe ye ñkpọ ntoro mmọdo ke ufọọd ndufo, kpa utọ a-adooho itịppeke ke atu mbon i-imiidiọọñọke Abasi. Se ñkop ado ke a-aba awodeen a-anieghe ewuana ye anwaan ete amọ. <verse eid="1CO 5:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="1CO 5:2" />Ado akappa ado ñkpọ ñkokkoidem inọ ndufo! Nte ikpinaaha efʌhọ ke esịd ndufo, enyʌñ ebịne awo a-anamma utọ ñkpọ ami esio ke atu ndufo? <verse eid="1CO 5:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="1CO 5:3" />Akpesʌkado a-ami mmembaaha do ye ndufo ke ikpọkidem, ami mmọdo ye ndufo ke sịbidịd. Ami mmebebiere ikpe nnọ andinam utọ ñkpọ ado, kpa nte ñkpekebaaha ke idem mmi. <verse eid="1CO 5:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="1CO 5:4" />Ndufo imaiboho ke anyịñ Abọọñ Yisọs ye ami ñko ke sịbidịd, adudu Abọọñ Yisọs anyʌñ aba do, <verse eid="1CO 5:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="1CO 5:5" />isaana utọ awo ami inọ Setan nọ ebiat abʌkidem amọ, nọ ato do edinyaaña sịbidịd amọ ke usen Abọọñ.<verse eid="1CO 5:5" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="1CO 5:6" />Ñkpooninua ndufo ifọnnọ. Ado nte ndufo idiọọñọke ke ataa etək yiis anam nọ ndomuyo atịt? <verse eid="1CO 5:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="1CO 5:7" />Isio akaan yiis ado ifep ke ufọọd ndufo, nọ ndufo edo ufa ndomuyo a-yiis imiisịneke, kpa naña ndufo enyʌñ eba. Sia e-ewa Krais, andido ayịnedọñ Usọrọ Nsaña Mboiyo ñnyịn. <verse eid="1CO 5:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="1CO 5:8" />Ke ntoro, yak ñnyịn inam adinam Usọrọ ami, idooho ye akaan uyo, e-esịnne yiis udu ye ibak, ado ye uyo a-yiis imiisịneke, uyo adisana esịd ye akpanikọ.<verse eid="1CO 5:8" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="1CO 5:9" />Ami mmaiwet ndufo ke ñwed mmi nte ikiinie ewuana ye mbon use, <verse eid="1CO 5:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="1CO 5:10" />ye mbon ederimbod ami e-edoññoke mme abʌd-abʌd ibon, mme adọrọitọñ, mbon ñwo, mme akpono ndem. Adinam ntoro, akpewuọñọ adiwuọ ñkpọñ ederimbod ami. <verse eid="1CO 5:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="1CO 5:11" />Ado ami ñwet idahami nte yak ndufo ikiinie ewuana ye awo a-adatta idem amọ nte ayịneka ke Krais<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">5:11 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Ke usem Greek adelfọi a-awuọñọke </char><char style="fq" closed="false">ayịneka </char><char style="fqa" closed="false">awodeen me awonwaan </char><char style="ft" closed="false">anyʌñ asʌk ada anọ awo a-anịmme Krais ke akpanikọ, me awodeen me awonwaan ke atu ubon Abasi; se ñko ke Rom 8:11, 13.</char></note> ado asịn efịbe, me anam use, me adọrọitọñ, me akpono ndem, me abiat awo anyịñ, me akpa mmịn, me anam ñwo. Ikiiwana kpak ukpọk ubọk ndidia ye utọ ibon ado.<verse eid="1CO 5:11" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="1CO 5:12" />Nsoo imbeghe miin adibiide ikpe nnọọ mbon i-imiibaaha ke esịd ufọkabasi? Nte inaaha ndufo ebiere ikpe enọ mbon e-ebaaha ke esịd ufọkabasi? <verse eid="1CO 5:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="1CO 5:13" />Abasi ayaakpe ikpe mbon e-ebaaha ke ederimbod. “Ibịne idiọọk awo isio ke atu ndufo.”<verse eid="1CO 5:13" /></para>
  <chapter eid="1CO 5" />
  <chapter number="6" style="c" sid="1CO 6" />
  <para style="s1">Ikpe ke Atu Nditọ Abasi</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="1CO 6:1" />Adieke keed ke atu ndufo anieghe utọk ye emọ-emọ, nte a-anen adiben mfịna ado ñkaa ikpe ke esob mbon i-imiidiọọñọke Abasi, utu ke eben eka iso ikọd Abasi? <verse eid="1CO 6:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="1CO 6:2" />Ado nte ndufo idiọọñọke ke ikọd Abasi ediikpe ikpe ederimbod? Ndin akpedo ndufo ediikpe ikpe ederimbod, ado nte ndufo ikanna ikpe ntək ikpe? <verse eid="1CO 6:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="1CO 6:3" />Ndufo idiọọñọke ke ñnyịn idiikpe ikpe inọ mme enyere? Nwaanwa dise mme ñkpọ uwem ederimbod ami! <verse eid="1CO 6:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="1CO 6:4" />Ke ntoro, adieke ndufo enieghe ntuaha ke mme ñkpọ ntom, nte a-anen adiben ikpe mbịne mbon e-eduuwem ammọ adooho ñkpọ nsaha ke esịd ufọkabasi? <verse eid="1CO 6:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="1CO 6:5" />Ntañ ami nọ abuud imʌm ndufo. Ado nte ibaaha awo ke atu ndufo a-anieghe aniọñ akem se akpe ikpe ke atu mme andinịm Abasi ke akpanikọ? <verse eid="1CO 6:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="1CO 6:6" />Utu ke ado, ayịneka aben ayịneka akaa ikpe ke esob, kpa ke iso mbon i-imiinịmme Abasi ke akpanikọ!<verse eid="1CO 6:6" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="1CO 6:7" />Ikpe adibaaba ke atu ndufo awọt ke ndufo ibaaha ufọn ndomokeed. Ntak afo umuuyakka nọ awo udue fiin-e? Ntak a-afo umuuyakka nọ awo utʌk fiin-e? <verse eid="1CO 6:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="1CO 6:8" />Utu ke ado, ndufo ke idem-idem ndufo emetʌk enyʌñ edue awo, enyʌñ enam ami ye nditọeka ndufo ke Krais. <verse eid="1CO 6:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="1CO 6:9" />Nte ndufo idiọọñọke ke mme anam idiọọk ndomokeed idiidʌkkọ abioubọọñ Abasi? Ikiiyak awo ibiaña ndufo: Mme anam use, ye mme akpono ndem, ye mme asịn efịbe, ye ideen e-enieghe ewuana ye emọ-emọ ideen, <verse eid="1CO 6:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="1CO 6:10" />mme inọ, ye mme akpammịn, ye mme abiambia, ye mbon ñwo idiinieghe udeeme ke abioubọọñ Abasi. <verse eid="1CO 6:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="1CO 6:11" />Se usʌk ndufo ekedo adodo. Ado emaiyet ndufo, enam esana, enyʌñ inọ unen ato ke anyịñ Abọọñ ñnyịn Yisọs Krais ye ke Sịbidịd Abasi ñnyịn.<verse eid="1CO 6:11" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Use ye Efịbe</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="1CO 6:12" />Afo abo, “Mmenie unen adinam ñkpọ akeedodo,” ado idooho afịd ñkpọ afọn. “Mmenie unen adinam ñkpọ akeedodo,” ado ndiidʌkkọ afʌn nnọ ñkpọ ndomokeed. <verse eid="1CO 6:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="1CO 6:13" />Afo abo “Ndidia ana anọ idịb, idịb ñko ana anọ ndidia, ado Abasi ayaasobo naña mmọ mba.” Ikpọkidem inaaha inọ use ye efịbe, ado ikpọkidem anie Abọọñ, ñko Abọọñ anie ikpọkidem. <verse eid="1CO 6:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="1CO 6:14" />Ke adudu amọ Abasi amaanam Abọọñ aset ke ñkpa. Anye ayaanam ñnyịn ñko iset ke ñkpa. <verse eid="1CO 6:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="1CO 6:15" />Nte ndufo idiọọñọke ke idem ndufo edoñño mme ñkek idem Krais? Nte ana ami mben mme ñkek idem Krais ñkedian ye mme akpara? Nwaaña nsa-o! <verse eid="1CO 6:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="1CO 6:16" />Nte ndufo idiọọñọke ke awo a-anieghe ewuana ye akpara akappa ado keed ye anye ke ikpọkidem? Sia e-ewet ete: “Iba eyaekappa edo abʌk keed.” <verse eid="1CO 6:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="1CO 6:17" />Ado awo a-adianna idem ye Abasi ado keed ye anye ke sịbidịd.<verse eid="1CO 6:17" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="1CO 6:18" />Feghe kpọñ use ye efịbe. Afịd ndiọiñkpọ mfen se awo anam, inamma ituuk idem amọ, ado awo a-anamma use ye efịbe a-anam idiọọkñkpọ a-atuuhọ idem amọ. <verse eid="1CO 6:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="1CO 6:19" />Nte ndufo idiọọñọke ke idem ndufo edo tembịd Adisana Sịbidịd i-isịneke ndufo ke idem, a-ndufo ekebọọhọ eto Abasi? Idooho ndufo enie idem ndufo; <verse eid="1CO 6:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="1CO 6:20" />ekidep ndufo ke ekọmudua. Ke ntoro, ikama idem ndufo inọ Abasi ukpono.<verse eid="1CO 6:20" /></para>
  <chapter eid="1CO 6" />
  <chapter number="7" style="c" sid="1CO 7" />
  <para style="s1">Ke Abaña Ndọ</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="1CO 7:1" />Ke abaña se ndufo ekewet ebịp: “A-afọn awodeen aditre inie ewuana ye awonwaan.” <verse eid="1CO 7:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="1CO 7:2" />Ado sia use ye efịbe ekponno eti-eti, yak awodeen keedekeed anie ewuana ye anwaan amọ, awonwaan anyʌñ anie ewuana ye ebe amọ. <verse eid="1CO 7:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="1CO 7:3" />Ebe ana anam ubiọñutom ndọ anọ anwaan amọ, anwaan ñko ana anam kpasʌk ntoro. <verse eid="1CO 7:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="1CO 7:4" />Anwaan inieghe adudu ibaña idem amọ, ado ana ayaak idem amọ anọ ebe amọ. Kpa ke ukem usʌñ ado, ebe inieghe adudu ibaña idem amọ, ado ana ayaak idem amọ anọ anwaan amọ. <verse eid="1CO 7:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="1CO 7:5" />Ikiinyịm emọ-emọ idem ndufo, ibọhọke ado ke unyịmme ndufo, ñko ke etək-etək ini, nọ ndufo ekan eyaak idem ndufo ayọhọ-ayọhọ esịn ke ubọñ akam. Imaikweñe imaana iba keed mbaak Setan adidomo ndufo idomo ato ke unana mfadidem. <verse eid="1CO 7:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="1CO 7:6" />Ntañ ami ke akikere mmi, idooho nte ewʌhọ. <verse eid="1CO 7:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="1CO 7:7" />Ami ñkpaama afịd ideen ekpeba nte ami. Ado awodeen keedekeed a-anie asaña-asaña enọ amọ ato Abasi; awo keed anie enọ anyem, awo mfen anie enọ mfen.<verse eid="1CO 7:7" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="1CO 7:8" />Yak ami ndọkkọ mbon i-imiidọọhọ ndọ<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">7:8 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Akeme inyʌñ ndo </char><char style="fqa" closed="false">awodeen a-anwaan amọ akpaaha</char></note> ye mme ebekpa nte ke a-afọn ammọ aditie nte ami, idọọhọ ndọ. <verse eid="1CO 7:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="1CO 7:9" />Ado akpedo ammọ ikanna inie mfadidem, yak ammọ edọ ndọ, sia a-afọn adidọ ndọ akan adikpa iwʌd.<verse eid="1CO 7:9" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="1CO 7:10" />Mmenọ mbon e-edọọhọ ndọ ewʌhọ ami (idooho ami, ado Abọọñ): Anwaan inaaha adiañña akpọñ ebe amọ. <verse eid="1CO 7:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="1CO 7:11" />Anye akpediañña ndọ, inaaha anye adọ ndọ aba, me idooho ntoro yak anye anam emem ye ebe amọ. Ebe ñko inaaha asio anwaan amọ ndọ.<verse eid="1CO 7:11" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="1CO 7:12" />Amaado mbon mfen, ami mbo nte (ami, idooho Abọọñ abo): Adieke ayịneka awodeen ke Krais anieghe anwaan i-imiinịmme Abasi ke akpanikọ, ado anwaan ado anyịmme adidʌñ ye anye, inaaha anye asio anye ndọ. <verse eid="1CO 7:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="1CO 7:13" />Awonwaan ñko akpenie ebe i-imiinịmme Abasi ke akpanikọ, ado ebe ado anyịmme adidʌñ ye anye, inaaha anye asio anye ndọ. <verse eid="1CO 7:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="1CO 7:14" />Sia e-enam ebe i-imiinịmme ke akpanikọ asana ato ke anwaan a-anịmme ke akpanikọ, ñko e-enam anwaan i-imiinịmme ke akpanikọ asana ato ke ebe a-anịmme ke akpanikọ. Miikpidooho ntoro, nditọ ndufo ekpedoñño mbubiam, ado naña aba ado, ammọ edoñño edisana.<verse eid="1CO 7:14" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="1CO 7:15" />Ado adieke anye i-imiinịmme ke akpanikọ awuọhọ ndọ, yak anye anyọñ. Akpetịppe ntoro, mbed ibọppọ nditọeka ke Krais e-enịmme ke akpanikọ sia Abasi abo yak ñnyịn idʌñ ke emem. <verse eid="1CO 7:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="1CO 7:16" />Afo anwaan, anam die adiọọñọ me afo uduunyaaña ebe mfo? Ñko, afo ebe, anam die adiọọñọ me afo uduunyaaña anwaan mfo?<verse eid="1CO 7:16" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Ke Abaña Ukpəho Ndaha</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="1CO 7:17" />Kpayeado, yak awo keedekeed adu uwem nte andinịm ke akpanikọ ke ndaha akeedodo ake Abọọñ anịmme anye akeene naña Abasi akekoot ammọ. Anye ami ado mbed a-ami nnịmme ke afịd ufọkabasi. <verse eid="1CO 7:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="1CO 7:18" />Nte emaefọfọọrọ awodeen edʌd ndin anye abọ ikood? Inaaha anye atịmme akedo afọọrọ edʌd. Nte awodeen akedo afọọrọ edʌd ini anye akebọọhọ ikood? Inaaha anye afọọrọ edʌd. <verse eid="1CO 7:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="1CO 7:19" />Adifọọrọ edʌd me aditre adifọọrọ edʌd idooho ñkpọ ndomokeed. Adinịm mbed Abasi ado akpan ñkpọ. <verse eid="1CO 7:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="1CO 7:20" />Yak awo aba ke ndaha a-anye akebaaha mbemiso anye abọ ikood Abasi.<verse eid="1CO 7:20" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="1CO 7:21" />Nte afo akedo afʌn idaha a-akebọọhọ ikood? Kuuyak ado ufịna fiin, ado adieke akanna awuọ ke ufʌn, nam ntoro. <verse eid="1CO 7:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="1CO 7:22" />Sia awo a-akedooho afʌn idaha a-anye akebọọhọ ikood ke Abọọñ, awuọ ke ufʌn ke ntak Abasi. Ke ukem usʌñ ado, awo a-akedooho amanaisọñ ke ini anye akebọọhọ ikood, ado afʌn Krais. <verse eid="1CO 7:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="1CO 7:23" />Ekidep ndufo ke ekọmudua; ikiido ifʌn inọọ mme awo. <verse eid="1CO 7:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="1CO 7:24" />Nditọeka ke Krais, yak awo keedekeed a-abọọrọke ikood Abasi, aba ke ndaha a-anye akebaaha ke ini Abasi akekootto anye.<verse eid="1CO 7:24" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Ke Abaña Mbon I-imiidọọhọ Ndọ</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" sid="1CO 7:25" />Ke abaña ndisịre ubọikpa, ami mbọọhọ ewʌhọ nto Abasi, ado mmenọ akikere mmi nte awo e-edatta nte anam akpanikọ ke mbọm Abasi. <verse eid="1CO 7:25" /><verse number="26" style="v" sid="1CO 7:26" />Ke ntak mfịna se iba idahami, ami ñkere ke a-afọn ndufo aditie naña ndufo etie ado. <verse eid="1CO 7:26" /><verse number="27" style="v" sid="1CO 7:27" />Nte amedọ ndọ? Kuuyem adiwuọ ke ndọ. Nte udọọhọ ndọ? Kuuyem anwaan. <verse eid="1CO 7:27" /><verse number="28" style="v" sid="1CO 7:28" />Ado adieke adọọhọ ndọ, afo unamma idiọọkñkpọ; adieke abọikpa adọọhọ ndọ, anye inamma idiọọkñkpọ. Ado mme adọ ndọ eyaenie uwak mfịna ke uwem ami, ndin ñyemme ndufo enie utọ mme mfịna ado.<verse eid="1CO 7:28" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" sid="1CO 7:29" />Nditọete, se ñnwana aditañ ado, ke ini anekke aməho. Tọọñọ ke ami, yak mbon se inie ibaan ndọ edu uwem nte mbon i-imiinieghe; <verse eid="1CO 7:29" /><verse number="30" style="v" sid="1CO 7:30" />mbon se ifʌhọ, nte mbon i-imiifʌhọke, mbon se idaara, nte mbon i-imiidaarake; mbon e-edeppe ñkpọ, nte idooho ammọ enie ñkpọ ado; <verse eid="1CO 7:30" /><verse number="31" style="v" sid="1CO 7:31" />mbon e-ekamake ñkpọ ederimbod enam ñkpọ, nte mbon i-imiibenne ukpọñ ammọ ikọọñ ke mme ñkpọ ado. Sia naña aba ami ederimbod ami asʌk aboiyo afep.<verse eid="1CO 7:31" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" sid="1CO 7:32" />Ami ñkpaama ndufo etre adiba ke ayeemensia. Awodeen i-imiidọọhọ anwaan asịn akikere amọ ke ñkpọ Abọọñ, naña anye akpekan anem Abọọñ esịd. <verse eid="1CO 7:32" /><verse number="33" style="v" sid="1CO 7:33" />Ado awodeen a-adọọhọ anwaan, asịn akikere amọ ke ñkpọ ederimbod, naña anye akpekan anem anwaan amọ esịd, <verse eid="1CO 7:33" /><verse number="34" style="v" sid="1CO 7:34" />ndin akikere amọ awawak afañ. Awonwaan i-imiidọọhọ ebe, me adisịre abọikpa, asịn akikere amọ ke ñkpọ Abọọñ. Anye ayem adiwa idem nnọọ Abọọñ ke ikpọkidem ye ke sịbidịd. Ado anwaan ndọ asịn akikere amọ ke ñkpọ ederimbod, naña anye akpekan anem ebe amọ esịd. <verse eid="1CO 7:34" /><verse number="35" style="v" sid="1CO 7:35" />Ntañ ami ke ufọn ndufo, idooho adibọbọp ndufo, ado nọ edu uwem ke eti usʌñ, inieghe ubakka ke esịd ke adinam ñkpọ nnọọ Abọọñ.<verse eid="1CO 7:35" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="36" style="v" sid="1CO 7:36" />Adieke awo ndomokeed akereke ke imọ idiikanna idu uwem a-adotto ye abọikpa a-anye ayemme idọ, ndin adieke iwʌd amọ anekkeke akpon, ndin anye akere ke akpena imọ idọ ndọ, yak anye anam ntoro. Anye inamma idiọọkñkpọ. Yak ammọ edudọiyọ. <verse eid="1CO 7:36" /><verse number="37" style="v" sid="1CO 7:37" />Ado adieke awo anamma ñkpembiere ke esịd amọ, awo ndomokeed imiinyʌññọ inyenyịk anye, ado anie iwuuk anyʌñ abiide ke imọ ibooho idọ abọikpa i-imiidiọọñọke awodeen akpa, awodeen ado ñko anam eti ñkpọ. <verse eid="1CO 7:37" /><verse number="38" style="v" sid="1CO 7:38" />Ke ntoro, andidọ abọikpa i-imiidiọọñọke awodeen akpa anam nnen-nnen ñkpọ, ado anye i-imiidọọhọ akap afọfọn akan.<verse eid="1CO 7:38" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="39" style="v" sid="1CO 7:39" />Awonwaan adiana ye ebe amọ adaña nte anye aduuho uwem. Ado adieke ebe amọ akpaaha, anye a-anie unen adidọ awo mfen a-anye amaaha, ado ana awo ado ado awo Abasi. <verse eid="1CO 7:39" /><verse number="40" style="v" sid="1CO 7:40" />Ke akikere mmi, anye ayaakop inemesịd akan, anye akpetre adidọ ndọ, anyʌñ atie naña anye aba. Mmekere ke ami ñko mmenie Sịbidịd Abasi.<verse eid="1CO 7:40" /></para>
  <chapter eid="1CO 7" />
  <chapter number="8" style="c" sid="1CO 8" />
  <para style="s1">Ke Abaña Ndidia e-Ewaaha Enọ Ndem</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="1CO 8:1" />Ke abaña ndidia e-ewaaha enọ mme ndem, ñnyịn imidiọọñọ ke afịd ñnyịn iminie ifiọk. Ndin ifiọk asaña ye ntañidem, ado ima abọbọp. <verse eid="1CO 8:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="1CO 8:2" />Awo a-akereke ke imọ imidiọọñọ ñkpọ, idiọọñọke ikikem naña anye akpediọọñọ. <verse eid="1CO 8:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="1CO 8:3" />Ado Abasi a-adiọọñọ awo a-amaaha anye.<verse eid="1CO 8:3" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="1CO 8:4" />Ke ntoro, ke abaña adidia ndidia e-ewaaha enọ mme ndem, ñnyịn imidiọọñọ “Ke ndem idooho ñkpọ ndomokeed ke ederimbod” ñko “Ke Abasi keed kpọd aba.” <verse eid="1CO 8:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="1CO 8:5" />Akpedodo mme “abasi” mfen ebañña, me ke anyọñ me ke ederimbod (kpa naña uwak mme “abasi” ye uwak “mbọọñ” ebañña), <verse eid="1CO 8:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="1CO 8:6" />ñnyịn inie Abasi keed kpọd, a-adooho Ete, a-afịd ñkpọ aketooho anye, a-ñnyịn inyʌññọ idu uwem inọọ. Ñko Abọọñ keed aba, kpa Yisọs Krais, a-afịd ñkpọ aketooho ke anye, a-ñnyịn inyʌññọ idu uwem ito kpa anye.<verse eid="1CO 8:6" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="1CO 8:7" />Ado idooho afịd awo ediọọñọ ami. Uwa ndem ameghe ubaak awo tutu ayedo ammọ emaedia ndidia uwa, ammọ edikere ke ado ndidia e-ekewaaha enọ ndem, ndin sia esịd ammọ adooho mmem-mmem, ndidia ado akappa ado ndubiam anọ ammọ. <verse eid="1CO 8:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="1CO 8:8" />Ado idooho ndidia anam nọ ñnyịn ikpere Abasi. Idiọọhọdiọọk ye ñnyịn adieke idiaaha, inyʌññọ ifọfọn ye ñnyịn ke ikpitre adidia.<verse eid="1CO 8:8" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="1CO 8:9" />Ado kpeme, mbaak mme unen mfo adido ñkpọiduọ anọọ awo mmemidem. <verse eid="1CO 8:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="1CO 8:10" />Sia awo mmem-mmem esịd akpekịt nte afo awo ifiọk adia ndidia ke itie ukpono ndem, nte ado ikemeke isọọñọ anye idem adidia ñkpọ e-ewaaha enọ ndem? <verse eid="1CO 8:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="1CO 8:11" />Ndin ayịneka ke Krais a-abaaha ke mmemidem, a-Krais akekpaaha anọ, akịt nsobo ato ke ifiọk mfo. <verse eid="1CO 8:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="1CO 8:12" />Afo umaunam nditọete e-enieghe mmem-mmem esịd edue ke utọ usʌñ ami, afo ñko amedue Krais. <verse eid="1CO 8:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="1CO 8:13" />Ke ntoro, adieke se ami ndia anamma nọ ayịneka mmi ke Krais anam idiọkñkpọ, ami ndiidiaha utọ ndidia ado aba tutu amama, mbaak ami ndinam ammọ eduọ.<verse eid="1CO 8:13" /></para>
  <chapter eid="1CO 8" />
  <chapter number="9" style="c" sid="1CO 9" />
  <para style="s1">Mme Unen Pọọl nte Abọsịd</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="1CO 9:1" />Nte ami ndooho amanaisọñ? Nte ami ndooho abọsịd? Nte ami ñkikịtte Yisọs Abọọñ ñnyịn? Nte idooho ndufo edo mfịd utom mmi ke Abọọñ? <verse eid="1CO 9:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="1CO 9:2" />Akpesʌkado mmeñkpedooho abọsịd nnọ mbon mfen, mmenịm ke mmedo inọ ndufo! Sia ndufo edo ufiikñkpọ abọsịd mmi ke Abọọñ.<verse eid="1CO 9:2" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="1CO 9:3" />Ibọọrọ se nnie nnọ mbon e-etieghe ke adimbiom miin ikpe ado ami. <verse eid="1CO 9:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="1CO 9:4" />Ado nte ñnyịn inieghe unen adidia ñnyʌñ ñnwọñ ñkpọ? <verse eid="1CO 9:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="1CO 9:5" />Ado nte ñnyịn inieghe unen adiben anwaan a-anịmme Abasi ke akpanikọ nsaña nnam utom, kpa naña mbed mbon ako ye nditọeka Abọọñ ye Kefas enañña? <verse eid="1CO 9:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="1CO 9:6" />Ado nte ami ye Banabas ikpọọñ imiinieghe unen aditre unam utom nọ idia ñkpọ?<verse eid="1CO 9:6" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="1CO 9:7" />Anie awo ikpe idem amọ akʌk inwana ekọñ? Anie awo akeme itọ inwañ ado idiaha utịb inwañ ado? Anie awo akpeme ufene ado inwọññọ mmọọñeba ufene ado? <verse eid="1CO 9:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="1CO 9:8" />Ado nte ami ntañ ami ke adudu abʌkidem? Nte Mbed itañña ukem ami? <verse eid="1CO 9:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="1CO 9:9" />Sia e-ewet ke Ñwed Mbed Moses ete: “Kuubọp abaakenañ inua ke ini anye akịmme isọñ utọ abakpa.” Ado nte abaakenañ ke Abasi akere ñkpọ abaña? <verse eid="1CO 9:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="1CO 9:10" />Ke akpanikọ anye atañ ami ibaña ñnyịn. Ii, anye atañ ibaña ñnyịn, sia andikịm isọñ amaakịm, andinuak isọñ anyʌñ anuak, enam ke idodanyen ke mmimọ iyaiwuana ke idọk ado. <verse eid="1CO 9:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="1CO 9:11" />Adieke adooho ñnyịn imitọ ñkpasi sịbidịd ke atu ndufo, nte anekke akpon abọhọ ñnyịn adidọk ñkpọ ikpọkidem ito ndufo? <verse eid="1CO 9:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="1CO 9:12" />Adieke mbon mfen enieghe unen adibọ utọ unwam ami ito ndufo, nte ñnyịn ikpikappa inekke inie unen adibọ unwam ami ikan ammọ? Ado ñnyịn ikikeeneke unen ami.</para>
  <para style="p" vid="1CO 9:12">Utu ke ado, ñnyịn ikaakappa iyọ se adodo mbaak idibiọọñọ eti etob Krais.<verse eid="1CO 9:12" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="1CO 9:13" />Nte ndufo idiọọñọke ke mbon e-enamma utom tembịd edia eto tembịd, ñko ke mbon e-enamma utom ke itie uwa ekeene ewuana ke ndidia uwa? <verse eid="1CO 9:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="1CO 9:14" />Kpa ke ukem usʌñ ado, Abọọñ anọ mbed ate mbon e-ekwọrọke eti etob ana edia ñkpọ eto eti etop.<verse eid="1CO 9:14" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="1CO 9:15" />Ado ami ndatta unen ami ndomokeed nnam ñkpọ. Ñnyʌññọ ñwet ewʌhọ ami nọ ato do ndufo enam mme ñkpọ ami ennọ miin. Sia ami mmenyịmme adikpikpa utu ke awo ndomokeed ambọọ miin unen adikpọ inua mbaña ñkpọ ami. <verse eid="1CO 9:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="1CO 9:16" />Ado ami ñkemeke adikpọ inua, ke ini ami ñkwọrọke eti etob Abasi, sia ana ami ñkwọrọ ikọ Abasi. Adọdiọọk annọ miin adieke ami mmiikwọrọke eti etob Abasi! <verse eid="1CO 9:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="1CO 9:17" />Adieke ami ñkwọrọke ke ini awo imiñnyịkkenyịk, mmenie ñkpọ ayịnutom, ado ekpeñnyenyịk atie nte nnam ubiọñutom a-anaaha nnam. <verse eid="1CO 9:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="1CO 9:18" />Nsoo ndin ido udodo mmi? Ukweeñe ado ke adikwọrọ eti etob Abasi mmekeme inam ado ke mfọn, ndin ñyịreke ke ayọhọ unen mmi nte akwọrọikọ Abasi.<verse eid="1CO 9:18" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Se Pọọl Akekama Ubọkkọ Amọ Anam</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="1CO 9:19" />Akpesʌkado ami mmendooho afʌn, ñnyʌññọ ndo inie awo ndomokeed, mmekappa nnam idem mmi afʌn nnọ afịd awo nọ ato do ñkọ uwak-uwak awo naña ñkpekakan nnọ Krais. <verse eid="1CO 9:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="1CO 9:20" />Mmeforo Yuu nnọ mme Yuu nọ ato do ñkọ mme Yuu. Mbon e-ebaaha ke idak mbed mmenyʌñ ñkappa ndo awo a-abaaha ke idak mbed (akpesʌkado a-ami mmembaaha ke idak mbed), nọ ato do ñkọ ukpọñ mbon e-ebaaha ke idak mbed. <verse eid="1CO 9:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="1CO 9:21" />Ami mmenyʌñ ñkappa ntie nte awo i-imiinieghe mbed nnọ mbon i-imiinieghe mbed (akpesʌkado ami mmembọkkọke mbed Abasi ado ami mba ke idak mbed Krais) nọ ato do ñkọ mbon i-miinieghe mbed. <verse eid="1CO 9:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="1CO 9:22" />Mmekappa ndo awo mmemidem nnọ mbon mmemidem, nọ ñkọ mbon mmemidem. Ami mmekappa ndo afịd ñkpọ nnọ afịd awo, nọ ato do ke usʌñ akeedodo ami ñnyaaña usʌk. <verse eid="1CO 9:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="1CO 9:23" />Ami nnam afịd ami ke ntak eti etob Abasi, nọ ato do ami ñkeene ñwana ke mme adidiọñ ami.<verse eid="1CO 9:23" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Adinie Mfarakeidem</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" sid="1CO 9:24" />Nte ndufo idiọọñọke ke nduba, afịd awo emia nduba, ado awo keed kpọd asibọ utịb? Ifeghe nọ ato do ebọ utịb. <verse eid="1CO 9:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="1CO 9:25" />Afịd awo se ika nduba ana enam ataa mbeeñeidem. Ammọ enam ami nọ ato do ebọ anyanya i-imiidiibaaha ke nsi-nsi; ado ñnyịn inam ami nọ ato do ibọ anyanya a-adiiba ke nsi-nsi nsi-nsi. <verse eid="1CO 9:25" /><verse number="26" style="v" sid="1CO 9:26" />Ke ntoro, ami mfegheke itọk nte awo i-imiinieghe iwuuk; ñnwanake anwan nte awo a-aduọọñọke aduọọñọ eta amọ. <verse eid="1CO 9:26" /><verse number="27" style="v" sid="1CO 9:27" />Iyoo, ami ntọ idem mmi eta, ñnyʌñ nnam anye ado afʌn mmi; nọ ato do ke ami mmaakwọrọ nnọ mbon mfen, ami ke idem mmi nsịneke ke atu mbon imiidiidotto adibọ utịb ado.<verse eid="1CO 9:27" /></para>
  <chapter eid="1CO 9" />
  <chapter number="10" style="c" sid="1CO 10" />
  <para style="s1">Ndʌdutọñ a-Atooho Mbʌkesed Nditọ Isrel</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="1CO 10:1" />Nditọeka ke Krais, ami ñyemme ndufo enana ifiọk ebaña mme eteete ñnyịn ekebaaha ke idak ntọñanyọñ, ke ammọ emaesaña eboiyo ke akpainyañ. <verse eid="1CO 10:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="1CO 10:2" />Ekeduọk afịd ammọ mmọọñ esịn ke Moses ke ntọñanyọñ ke akpainyañ. <verse eid="1CO 10:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="1CO 10:3" />Afịd ammọ ekedia ukem ndidia sịbidịd keed, <verse eid="1CO 10:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="1CO 10:4" />ndin emaenyʌñ enwọñ ñkpọ eto itiad sịbidịd, a-akesañake ye ammọ; ndin itiad ado akedo Krais. <verse eid="1CO 10:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="1CO 10:5" />Kpayeado, Abasi ikinemme esịd ye uwak ammọ, ndin emaesuan akpo ammọ ke akpautatan.<verse eid="1CO 10:5" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="1CO 10:6" />Mme ñkpọ ami eketịppe nọ ado ukpeebñkpọ inọ ñnyịn; nọ itre adisịn esịd ñnyịn ke ndiọiñkpọ naña mbon ado ekenam. <verse eid="1CO 10:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="1CO 10:7" />Ikiido mme akpono ndem, naña ubaak ammọ ekedo. E-ewet ebo ke “Ammọ emaesuuk etie edia ñkpọ, enyʌñ enwọñ enyʌñ ekeene ewuana ke mme atịme ye mbubiam ido.” <verse eid="1CO 10:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="1CO 10:8" />Inaaha ñnyịn inam use kpa naña usʌk ammọ ekenam, a-akenamma tọsịn edịb mme ita ekpañña ke usen keed. <verse eid="1CO 10:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="1CO 10:9" />Inaaha ñnyịn idomo Krais idomo naña usʌk ammọ ekenam, ndin udʌkikọd amaakọñ ammọ awoot. <verse eid="1CO 10:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="1CO 10:10" />Yak ñnyịn ñko ikiidukuunọ, naña usʌk ammọ ekedukuunọ, ndin enyere nsobo asobo ammọ.<verse eid="1CO 10:10" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="1CO 10:11" />Mme ñkpọ ami eketịppe anọ ammọ nte ukpeebñkpọ, ndin e-ewet enịm nte ñkpọ ndʌdutọñ inọ ñnyịn mbon e-enieghe idodanyen utịd ini iso. <verse eid="1CO 10:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="1CO 10:12" />Ke ntoro, adieke afo akereke ke imọ imisọọñọ ida, nekke kpeme idem mbaak afo ududuọ! <verse eid="1CO 10:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="1CO 10:13" />Idomo ndomokeed isịmme ndufo a-adooho kpaanam isịmme awo mfen. Abasi ado anam akpanikọ; anye idiiyakka idomo a-akponno ikan ndufo isịm ndufo. Idomo amaadi anye ayaasio usʌñ nọ ato do ekan eyọ idomo ado.<verse eid="1CO 10:13" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Mme Usọrọ Ndem ye Ndidia Abọọñ</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="1CO 10:14" />Ke ntoro mme ndima ufan mmi, ifeeñe ikpọñ ukpono ndem. <verse eid="1CO 10:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="1CO 10:15" />Ami ntañ ikọ nnọ mme adiọọñọidem awo, ndin idomo se ami ntañ ise. <verse eid="1CO 10:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="1CO 10:16" />Nte kọọb ekọọm a-ñnyịn inọọhọ ekọọm idooho ewuana ke iyiib Krais? Nte uyo a-ñnyịn ibuuñọ idooho ewuana ke ikpọkidem Krais? <verse eid="1CO 10:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="1CO 10:17" />Sia idem uyo keed aba, ndin ñnyịn ñko, akpesʌkado i-idooho uwak, ido idem keed, sia afịd ñnyịn iwana ke eboho uyo keed ado.<verse eid="1CO 10:17" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="1CO 10:18" />Kere baña mbon Isrel: Nte mbon e-ediaha ndidia uwa inieghe ewuana ke itie uwa? <verse eid="1CO 10:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="1CO 10:19" />Nte ami mbo ke uwa e-ewaaha enọ ndem awuọñọ ñkpọ ndomokeed, me ndem ado ñkpọ ndomokeed? <verse eid="1CO 10:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="1CO 10:20" />Iyoo, ado mme uwa a-mbon i-imiidiọọñọke Abasi ewaaha, ewa ammọ enọ mme dimọn, iwaaha inọ Abasi, ndin ami ñyemme ndufo enie ewuana ye mme dimọn. <verse eid="1CO 10:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="1CO 10:21" />Ndufo ikemeke adinwọñ kọọb Abasi ndian ye kọọb mme dimọn; ndufo ikemeke adinie ewuana ke akpokoro Abasi ye ke akpokoro mme dimọn. <verse eid="1CO 10:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="1CO 10:22" />Ado nte ñnyịn iyem adinam <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> afịbe ufịb? Nte ñnyịn iminie inweek ikan Abasi?<verse eid="1CO 10:22" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Ñkpọkñyak mme Andinịm ke Akpanikọ</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" sid="1CO 10:23" />Afo ate “Mmekan adinam afịd ñkpọ,” ado idooho afịd ñkpọ anie ufọn. “Mmekan adinam afịd ñkpọ,” ado idooho afịd ñkpọ awuọñọ ñkpọ. <verse eid="1CO 10:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="1CO 10:24" />Awo ndomokeed inaaha ayem ufọn idem amọ, ado ana ayem ufọn mbon mfen.<verse eid="1CO 10:24" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" sid="1CO 10:25" />Dia ñkpọ ndidia akeedodo e-enyamma ke udua; kuubịp mbịme ubaña, nọ ato do esịd mfo ana inwañ-inwañ. <verse eid="1CO 10:25" /><verse number="26" style="v" sid="1CO 10:26" />Sia, “ederimbod anie Abọọñ, ye afịd ñkpọ se idọñọ ke esịd.”<verse eid="1CO 10:26" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" sid="1CO 10:27" />Adieke awo i-imiinịmme Abasi ke akpanikọ ukoodo fiin ndidia, dia ñkpọ akeedodo e-enịmme ke iso mfo; kuubịp mbịme a-aketuuho akikere esịd. <verse eid="1CO 10:27" /><verse number="28" style="v" sid="1CO 10:28" />Ado adieke awo ubooho fiin ate, “Ñkpọ ami ado ñkpọ uwa,” kuudia ke ntak awo se udọkkọ fiin ye ke ntak akikere esịd. <verse eid="1CO 10:28" /><verse number="29" style="v" sid="1CO 10:29" />Ami ntañ ke ntak esịd awo ado, idooho ke ntak ake mfo. Sia ntak a-akikere esịd awo mfen akpebiideke ikpe abaña ubọkkọ mmi-e? <verse eid="1CO 10:29" /><verse number="30" style="v" sid="1CO 10:30" />Adieke ami ñwanake ke ndidia ado ye esịd ekọọm, ntak a-ami ñkpenieghe ubiomikpe ke ñkpọ a-ami nnọọhọ Abasi ekọọm-ọ?<verse eid="1CO 10:30" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" sid="1CO 10:31" />Ke ntoro, me afo adiadia me anwọọnwọñ, se adoodo a-afo anamma, nam dịppe ubọọñ Abasi. <verse eid="1CO 10:31" /><verse number="32" style="v" sid="1CO 10:32" />Kuunam nọ awo mfen aduọ, me Yuu, me Gentile, me ufọkabasi, <verse eid="1CO 10:32" /><verse number="33" style="v" sid="1CO 10:33" />kpa naña ami ñnwana inam afịd awo ekop inemesịd ke afịd usʌñ. Sia ami ñyemme ufọn nnọ idem mmi, ado ñyem ufọn uwak awo, nọ ato do ammọ ebọ adinyaaña.<verse eid="1CO 10:33" /></para>
  <chapter eid="1CO 10" />
  <chapter number="11" style="c" sid="1CO 11" />
  <para style="nb">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="1CO 11:1" />Ikeene uwọdñkpọ mmi kpa naña ami ñkeene uwọdñkpọ Krais.<verse eid="1CO 11:1" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Ke Abaña Ufʌk Iwuod ke Ufọkabasi</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="1CO 11:2" />Ami mmitooro ndufo ke adintoiyo miin ke afịd ñkpọ ye adimʌm mme ndutʌm ñkpọ Abasi ñkama kpa naña ñkekpọñ ammọ inọọ ndufo. <verse eid="1CO 11:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="1CO 11:3" />Idahami, ñyem ndufo ediọọñọ ke Krais ado iwuod anọ awodeen, ñko awodeen ado iwuod anọ awonwaan, ndin Abasi ado iwuod anọ Krais. <verse eid="1CO 11:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="1CO 11:4" />Awodeen akeedodo a-abọññọ akam me a-atañ prọfesi ke ini anye afʌkkọ iwuod amọ, a-amiom iwuod amọ. <verse eid="1CO 11:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="1CO 11:5" />Ñko awonwaan akeedodo a-abọññọ akam me a-atañ prọfesi ke ini anye imiifʌkkọ iwuod amọ, a-amiom iwuod amọ, atie ukem nte anye adifat ided amọ. <verse eid="1CO 11:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="1CO 11:6" />Sia adieke awonwaan imiifʌkkọ iwuod amọ akpena anye afat ided amọ; ado akpedo ado ñkpọ abuud anye adifat ided, yak anye afʌk iwuod.<verse eid="1CO 11:6" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="1CO 11:7" />Awodeen ikpinaaha afʌk iwuod amọ sia anye ado mbid ye ubọọñ Abasi; ado awonwaan ado ubọọñ awodeen. <verse eid="1CO 11:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="1CO 11:8" />Sia awodeen ikitooho awonwaan idi, ado awonwaan aketo awodeen adi; <verse eid="1CO 11:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="1CO 11:9" />awo ikinyʌññọ ibot awodeen inọ awonwaan, ado ekebot awonwaan enọ awodeen. <verse eid="1CO 11:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="1CO 11:10" />Ke ntak ami, ye ke ntak mme enyere, ke ana awonwaan anie unen ke iwuod amọ. <verse eid="1CO 11:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="1CO 11:11" />Ado ke Abọọñ, awonwaan inieghe unen idem amọ ikpọñ awodeen; awodeen ñko inieghe unen idem amọ ikpọñ awonwaan. <verse eid="1CO 11:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="1CO 11:12" />Sia kpa naña awonwaan aketo awodeen, ntoro ñko, ke awodeen amana ato awonwaan. Ado afịd ñkpọ ato Abasi.<verse eid="1CO 11:12" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="1CO 11:13" />Ibiide inọ idem ndufo ise: Nte a-adot awonwaan adibọñ akam nnọọ Abasi ke ini iwuod amọ anaaha inwañ? <verse eid="1CO 11:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="1CO 11:14" />Nte edu ubonoñkpọ ikpeebe ñnyịn ke awodeen akpenie anyan ided, ado ñkpọ abuud anọ anye, <verse eid="1CO 11:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="1CO 11:15" />ado ke awonwaan akpenie anyan ided, ado uku amọ? Sia enọ anye anyan ided nte ufʌhọñkpọ. <verse eid="1CO 11:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="1CO 11:16" />Awo akpenie mfaaña abaña ñkpọ ami, ñnyịn inieghe ido mfen ikan ami, mme ufọkabasi ñko inyʌññọ inie.<verse eid="1CO 11:16" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Ndʌtutọñ ke Baña Edu Unam Ñkpọ ke Ini Ndidia Abọọñ</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="1CO 11:17" />Ke mme ewʌhọ ami, ami nnieghe itooro ndomokeed inọ ndufo, sia mme mbono ndufo a-anam idiọọk akan eti. <verse eid="1CO 11:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="1CO 11:18" />Ke akpa ifed, mmekop ke ndufo imaiboho ke ufọkabasi, ubakka a-aba ke atu ndufo, ndin mmeyem adinịm ke akpanikọ. <verse eid="1CO 11:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="1CO 11:19" />Kpayeado, ana ubakka aba ke atu ndufo nọ ediọọñọ mbon e-edooho ataa nditọ Abasi. <verse eid="1CO 11:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="1CO 11:20" />Ndufo imaiboho keed, idooho ndidia Abọọñ ke ndufo edia, <verse eid="1CO 11:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="1CO 11:21" />sia ndufo imaidia ñkpọ, usʌk ndufo idaaha ibet mbon mfen nọ edikeene edia. Ado anam ke ini awo keed adiaha ayʌkkọ, awo mfen adakka abiọọñ, ndin ukọd ananaam awo mfen. <verse eid="1CO 11:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="1CO 11:22" />Ado nte ndufo inieñeke ufọk se ndufo edia enyʌñ enwọñ ñkpọ? Me ado nte ndufo emiom ufọkabasi ke edisuenne mbon i-imiinieghe ñkpọ? Nsoo ke ami ndiitañ ye ndufo? Ado se ami itotooro ndufo? Ñkemekekeme itoro ndufo ke ñkpọ anyem!<verse eid="1CO 11:22" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" sid="1CO 11:23" />Sia se ami ñkebọọ ke ubọk Abọọñ ke ñkenyʌñ ñkpọñ inọọ ndufo. Abọọñ Yisọs ke akonayio e-eketappa anye enọ ñkpa, amaaben uyo, <verse eid="1CO 11:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="1CO 11:24" />ndin ke amaakenọ ekọọm, anye amaabuuñ uyo ado ate, <char style="wj">“Ikpọkidem mmi ado ami, i-inieghe ndufo; inam ami adidat intoiyo miin.”</char> <verse eid="1CO 11:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="1CO 11:25" />Kpa ke ukem usʌñ ado, ke emaekedia ndidia ndubi ema, anye amaaben kọọb ate, <char style="wj">“kọọb ami ado ufa edioomo ke iyiib mmi; inam ami, ini akeedodo a-ndufo enwọññọ ami, adidat intoiyo miin.”</char> <verse eid="1CO 11:25" /><verse number="26" style="v" sid="1CO 11:26" />Sia ini akeedodo a-ndufo etaaha uyo ami enyʌñ enwọñ kọọb ami, ndufo emesian ñkpa Abọọñ tutu anye atịmme adi.<verse eid="1CO 11:26" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" sid="1CO 11:27" />Ke ntoro, awo akeedodo a-ataaha uyo ami, me a-anyʌññọ anwọñ kọọb Abọọñ ke usʌñ i-imiidotto, a-anam idiọọkñkpọ abaña ikpọkidem ye iyiib Abọọñ. <verse eid="1CO 11:27" /><verse number="28" style="v" sid="1CO 11:28" />Akpena afịd awo eduuñọ idem ammọ ese mbemiso ammọ eta uyo enyʌñ enwọñ kọọb ado. <verse eid="1CO 11:28" /><verse number="29" style="v" sid="1CO 11:29" />Sia mbon se idia inyʌñ inwọñ ke ini ammọ imiikiduuñọke ikpọkidem Krais, e-edia enyʌñ enwọñ ubiomikpe enọ idem ammọ. <verse eid="1CO 11:29" /><verse number="30" style="v" sid="1CO 11:30" />Anye ado ntak u-uwak ke atu ndufo ekoppo mmemidem enyʌñ edọñọ, usʌk ndufo enyʌñ edaiya. <verse eid="1CO 11:30" /><verse number="31" style="v" sid="1CO 11:31" />Ado adieke ñnyịn ikpiduuñọke idem ñnyịn ise ñnyịn ikpibaaha ke utọ ubiomikpe ado. <verse eid="1CO 11:31" /><verse number="32" style="v" sid="1CO 11:32" />Kpayeado, ke ini Abọọñ akpeeghe ikpe inọọ ñnyịn ke utọ usʌñ ami, ñnyịn ibọ ntʌnọ mbaak ke akpatre edidian ñnyịn ye mbon ederimbod esobo.<verse eid="1CO 11:32" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="33" style="v" sid="1CO 11:33" />Ke ntoro, nditọeka mmi ke Krais, imaidiboho itie keed adidia ndidia, ana eda ebet emọ-emọ. <verse eid="1CO 11:33" /><verse number="34" style="v" sid="1CO 11:34" />Adieke abiọọñ adọññọ awo ndomokeed, yak anye adia ñkpọ ke ufọk amọ, mbaak adisoobo ndufo adido ke ubiomikpe.</para>
  <para style="p" vid="1CO 11:34">Ndin ami mmaatịmme ndi, ñyaamaana nnọ mme item mfen.<verse eid="1CO 11:34" /></para>
  <chapter eid="1CO 11" />
  <chapter number="12" style="c" sid="1CO 12" />
  <para style="s1">Mme Enọ Sịbidịd</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="1CO 12:1" />Nditọeka ke Krais, ami ñyemme ndufo enana ifiọk ebaña mme enọ Sịbidịd. <verse eid="1CO 12:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="1CO 12:2" />Ndufo emediọọñọ ke idaha a-ndufo ekedoññoke mbon i-imiikidiọọñọke Abasi, ndufo ekenam ñkpọ ekeene ndadusʌñ usọsọiñkpọ. <verse eid="1CO 12:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="1CO 12:3" />Ke ntoro, ami ibo ndufo ke ibaaha awo a-atañña ikọ ke ndadusʌñ Sịbidịd Abasi a-akemeke ibo “Adọdiọọk anọ Yisọs,” ndin awo ndomokeed idinyʌññọ ikan ibo, “Yisọs ado Abọọñ,” ke imiibọhọke ato Adisana Sịbidịd.<verse eid="1CO 12:3" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="1CO 12:4" />Mme nsio-nsio enọ ebañña, ado Sịbidịd keed adeeme afịd ammọ. <verse eid="1CO 12:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="1CO 12:5" />Nsio-nsio utom ebañña, ado Abọọñ ado keed. <verse eid="1CO 12:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="1CO 12:6" />Nsio-nsio adinam ebañña ado kpa Abasi keed anam afịd utom ke idem afịd awo.<verse eid="1CO 12:6" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="1CO 12:7" />E-enọ awo keedekeed enọ Sịbidịd nọ ato do anam ufọn anọ afịd awo. <verse eid="1CO 12:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="1CO 12:8" />Ato ke Sịbidịd enọ awo keed etob aniọñ, enọ awo mfen etob ifiọk kpasʌk ke Sịbidịd keed ado, <verse eid="1CO 12:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="1CO 12:9" />enọ awo mfen mbuọdidem kpa ke Sịbidịd keed ado, enọ awo mfen mme enọ ukọk mme udọñọ kpa ke Sịbidịd keed ado, <verse eid="1CO 12:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="1CO 12:10" />awo mfen enọ mme utịppe adudu, awo mfen enọ utañ prọfesi, awo mfen enọ adiduuñọ mme sịbidịd, awo mfen enọ enọ utañ nsio-nsio edemeikọ, awo mfen enyʌñ enọ enọ adikappa mme nsio-nsio edemeikọ. <verse eid="1CO 12:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="1CO 12:11" />Afịd ami ado utom Sịbidịd keed ami, anye anyʌñ adeeme awo keedekeed akeene naña anye ama.<verse eid="1CO 12:11" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Idem Keed, Uwak Ndido</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="1CO 12:12" />Kpa naña idem ado keed ado anie uwak ndido, ndin afịd uwak ndido edo idem keed, kpa ntoro ke ado ye Krais. <verse eid="1CO 12:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="1CO 12:13" />Sia ekiduọk afịd ñnyịn mmọọñ ke Sịbidịd keed nọ ñnyịn ikappa ido idem keed, me ido mme Yuu me mme Gentile, afʌn me amanaisọñ, ekenyʌñ inọ afịd ñnyịn Sịbidịd keed ami inwọñ. <verse eid="1CO 12:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="1CO 12:14" />Kpayeado idem inieghe ndido keed, anie uwak ndido.<verse eid="1CO 12:14" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="1CO 12:15" />Adieke ukod akpebooho ate, “Sia ami mmiidooho ubọk, ami ndooho mbaak idem,” ado idiinama anye atre adido ndido idem. <verse eid="1CO 12:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="1CO 12:16" />Adieke utọñ akpebooho ate, “Sia ami mmiidooho anyen, ami ndooho mbaak idem,” ibooho ito ke ntak ado anye atre adido ndido idem. <verse eid="1CO 12:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="1CO 12:17" />Adieke afịd idem akpedooho anyen, ekpenam die ekop ñkpọ? Adieke afịd idem akpedooho utọñ, ekpenam die enuuno ñkpọ? <verse eid="1CO 12:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="1CO 12:18" />Ado ke akpanikọ Abasi akeneeñe mme ndido abono ke idem, keedekeed, kpa naña anye akeyem nọ ammọ eba. <verse eid="1CO 12:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="1CO 12:19" />Adieke afịd ndido ekpedooho ndido keed kpọd, idem ndin akpeba ke mmọ? <verse eid="1CO 12:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="1CO 12:20" />Naña aba ado, ndido e-ewak, ado idem ado keed.<verse eid="1CO 12:20" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="1CO 12:21" />Anyen ikanna adibo ubọk “Ami uyemme fiin!” Iwuod ñko ikanna adibo ukod, “Ami uyemme fiin!” <verse eid="1CO 12:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="1CO 12:22" />Utu ke ado, mme ndido idem e-ebaaha nte ammọ edo se imem ikan, ammọ ekap edo se enekke eyem, <verse eid="1CO 12:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="1CO 12:23" />ndin mme ndido idem se ñnyịn ikere ke idooho se awo akịt ke ñnyịn ikappa inọọ asaña-asaña ukpono. Mme ndido idem a-awo imiibenne isio inyan edo mbon se ekama ukpono-ukpono, <verse eid="1CO 12:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="1CO 12:24" />ke ini adooho ndido idem se ekịt inieghe utọ asaña-asaña ukpono ado. Ado Abasi a-akoono mme nsio-nsio ndido idem abok keed, akappa aben akaakan ukpono anọ mme ndido i-imiikinieghe, <verse eid="1CO 12:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="1CO 12:25" />mbaak ubakka ndomokeed adiba ke afịd idem, ado anam mme ndido ekere ñkpọ ebaña emọ-emọ. <verse eid="1CO 12:25" /><verse number="26" style="v" sid="1CO 12:26" />Adieke ndido keed anieghe mfịna, afịd ndido enie mfịna ado ye anye; adieke ndido keed abọọhọ ukpono, afịd ndido edaara ye anye.<verse eid="1CO 12:26" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" sid="1CO 12:27" />Ndin ndufo edo idem Krais, ndufo keedekeed edo ndido idem ado. <verse eid="1CO 12:27" /><verse number="28" style="v" sid="1CO 12:28" />Ndin ke ufọkabasi, Abasi a-amek, ke akpa itie, mme abọsịd, udiana, mme prọfed, ayọhọ ita, mme andikpeeb, ndin mme anam utịppeñkpọ, ndin mbon se inie mme enọ ukọk udọñọ, mbon e-ekemeke inwam mbon mfen, mbon e-enieghe enọ ndadusʌñ, ye mbon e-enieghe nsio-nsio edeme ikọ. <verse eid="1CO 12:28" /><verse number="29" style="v" sid="1CO 12:29" />Nte afịd awo edoñño mme abọsịd? Afịd edoñño mme prọfed? Me afịd awo enam utịppeñkpọ? <verse eid="1CO 12:29" /><verse number="30" style="v" sid="1CO 12:30" />Me afịd enie mme enọ ukọk udọñọ? Nte afịd esem nsio-nsio edeme ikọ? Nte afịd ekan ekappa mme edeme ikọ? <verse eid="1CO 12:30" /><verse number="31" style="v" sid="1CO 12:31" />Ndin ñyem ndufo enekke eyem mme enọ se ifọn ikan afịd mme enọ mfen.</para>
  <para style="s1" vid="1CO 12:31">Ima Ado Akaakan Ñkpọ</para>
  <para style="p" vid="1CO 12:31">Ndin ami ñyaiwọt ndufo ataa eti usʌñ a-afọnnọ akan.<verse eid="1CO 12:31" /></para>
  <chapter eid="1CO 12" />
  <chapter number="13" style="c" sid="1CO 13" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="1CO 13:1" />Adieke ami nsemme usem mme awo ye ake mme enyere, ado nnieghe ima, ami nnam uyom nte akpañkpañ. <verse eid="1CO 13:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="1CO 13:2" />Adieke ami nnieghe enọ prọfesi ñnyʌñ ñkan ndiọọñọ mme ndịbe-ndịbe ñkpọ ye ifiọk, mmaana nnie mbuọdidem a-akemeke idịppe mme ikpọabod, ado nnieghe ima, awuọñọ ikpu-ikpu. <verse eid="1CO 13:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="1CO 13:3" />Adieke ami mbenne afịd inie mmi nnọ mme uweene, ñnyʌñ ñyaak idem mmi nnọ nsọñọñkpọ nọ ami ñwọk inua, ado nnieghe ima, udod indoroke miin ndomokeed.<verse eid="1CO 13:3" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="1CO 13:4" />Ima ado ime, ima afọfọn ido. Inieghe udu, inyʌññọ iduaak inua, ikokkoke idem. <verse eid="1CO 13:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="1CO 13:5" />Inanake ukpono inọ mbon mfen, iyemme ufọn idem amọ, isọppọ iyadesịd, ibatta nnamndue. <verse eid="1CO 13:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="1CO 13:6" />Ima ikoppo inem ke idiọọk, ado adaara ke akpanikọ. <verse eid="1CO 13:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="1CO 13:7" />Ima akpekpeme afịd ini, anịm ke akpanikọ, anie idodanyen, anie nsọọñọnda.<verse eid="1CO 13:7" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="1CO 13:8" />Ima akenanam ikpuuho. Ado ke itie nte mme prọfesi eba, ammọ eyaetre; itie nte nsio-nsio usem ebañña, eyaedobo; itie nte ifiọk aba, ayaaboiyo afep. <verse eid="1CO 13:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="1CO 13:9" />Sia ñnyịn idiọọñọ ñkpọ ubaak-ubaak, inyʌñ itañ prọfesi ubaak-ubaak, <verse eid="1CO 13:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="1CO 13:10" />ado ayọhọ ifiọk amaadi, se ido ubaak ifiọk ayaasop. <verse eid="1CO 13:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="1CO 13:11" />Idaha a-ami ñkedooho etəkayịn, ñketañ ikọ nte etəkayịn, ñkekere ñkpọ nte etəkayịn, ñkpọ akeñnwaña miin nte etəkayịn. Ke ini ami mmaakekpon ñwuọ ayọhọ awodeen, ami mmaayaak mme ñkpọ ntəkayịn nnịm. <verse eid="1CO 13:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="1CO 13:12" />Sia idahami ñnyịn ikịt ñkpọ ndukpọñ-ndukpọñ nte ikịt ke ukịdiso; ini amaakem iyaikịt iso ye iso. Idahami ami ndiọọñọ ñkpọ ubaak-ubaak; idahado ñyaadiọọñọ ayọhọ-ayọhọ, kpa naña endiọọñọ miin ayọhọ-ayọhọ.<verse eid="1CO 13:12" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="1CO 13:13" />Ndin idahami, ñkpọ ita esʌhọ: Mbuọdidem, idodanyen ye ima. Ado andikpon ñkan ke atu mme ñkpọ ami ado ima.<verse eid="1CO 13:13" /></para>
  <chapter eid="1CO 13" />
  <chapter number="14" style="c" sid="1CO 14" />
  <para style="s1">Ukpono Abasi Asaña ye Ikike</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="1CO 14:1" />Saña ke usʌñ ima nyʌñ nekke wʌdọ mme enọ Sịbidịd, akpan-akpan enọ prọfesi. <verse eid="1CO 14:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="1CO 14:2" />Sia awo akeedodo a-asemme nsio-nsio edemeikọ isemme inọ awo ado asem anọ Abasi. Ke akpanikọ, inwañake awo ndomokeed se ammọ esem sia ammọ esem mme ndedịbe ñkpọ ke Sịbidịd. <verse eid="1CO 14:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="1CO 14:3" />Ado awo a-atañña prọfesi atañ anọ mme awo nọ enie nsọọñọnda, nsọọñọidem ye idọñesịd. <verse eid="1CO 14:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="1CO 14:4" />Awo a-asemme nsio-nsio edemeikọ, asem ke ufọn idem amọ, ado awo a-atañña prọfesi atañ ke ufọn ufọkabasi. <verse eid="1CO 14:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="1CO 14:5" />Ami ñkpaama nọ afịd ndufo esem nsio-nsio edemeikọ, ado ñkpaanekke ñyem ndufo etañ prọfesi. Awo a-atañña prọfesi a-akoñ idaha akan awo a-semme nsio-nsio edemeikọ, ibọhọke aba awo se ikappa nọ anam ufọkabasi akọt.<verse eid="1CO 14:5" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="1CO 14:6" />Ndin, nditọeka ke Krais, adieke ami ndiighe ibịne ndufo ñnyʌñ nsem nsio-nsio edemeikọ, nsoo ufọn ke ami ndiinie inọọ ndufo, ibọhọke ami mben adiyaara me ifiọk me brọfesi me ukpeebñkpọ isọk ndufo? <verse eid="1CO 14:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="1CO 14:7" />Ikpidat udomo ñkpọ ke mme ñkpọ se ikeme adinam uyom nte adʌk me ndido, awo adiinam die idiọọñọ se ekwọ adieke anye imiidiọọñọke mme nsio-nsio uyio se idọñọ ke esịd? <verse eid="1CO 14:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="1CO 14:8" />Ñko, adieke uyio adukpoñ imiinwañake awo, ediinam die inie mbeeñeidem inọ ekọñ? <verse eid="1CO 14:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="1CO 14:9" />Ukem ami ke ado ye ndufo. Ibọhọke ndufo ekama edeme ndufo etañ ikọ se inwaña awo, ediinam die idiọọñọ se ndufo etañ? Adiiba nte ndufo etañ ikọ edọñ ke afịm. <verse eid="1CO 14:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="1CO 14:10" />Ado akpanikọ ke nsio-nsio usem ebañña ke ederimbod, ado ibaaha anye i-imiinieghe se awuọñọ. <verse eid="1CO 14:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="1CO 14:11" />Adieke mmeñkoppo se awo atañ, ami ndo asenawo nnọ awo ado, anye ñko ado asenawo annọ miin. <verse eid="1CO 14:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="1CO 14:12" />Ukem ami ke ado ye ndufo. Sia ndufo enieghe udọñ adinie mme enọ Sịbidịd, idomo ukeme adinekke nnam ufọkabasi akọt.<verse eid="1CO 14:12" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="1CO 14:13" />Ke ntak ado, yak mbon e-esemme nsio-nsio edemeikọ ebọñ akam ebeeñe ukeme adikan ñkappa se ammọ esem. <verse eid="1CO 14:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="1CO 14:14" />Sia adieke ami mbọññọ akam ke asen edemeikọ, ado sịbidịd mmi abọñ akam, ado esịd mmi inieghe mbunwịm. <verse eid="1CO 14:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="1CO 14:15" />Ndin ami ndiinam die? Ana mbọñ akam ke sịbidịd mmi ñnyʌñ mbọñ ke ikike mmi ñko; ana ñkwọ ikwọ ke sịbidịd mmi ñnyʌñ ñkwọ ke ikike mmi ñko. <verse eid="1CO 14:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="1CO 14:16" />Adieke afo atooroke Abasi ke sịbidịd mfo, mbon mfen e-etooho esiin edi ediinam die isọọñọ ekọọm mfo ke adibo, “Amen” ke ini ammọ imiidiọọñọke se afo atañ? <verse eid="1CO 14:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="1CO 14:17" />Afo anọ ekọọm ke akpanikọ, ado ekọọm mfo ibaaha ufọn inọ awo mfen.<verse eid="1CO 14:17" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="1CO 14:18" />Mmekọọm Abasi ke ami mmesem nsio-nsio edemeikọ ñkan afịd ndufo. <verse eid="1CO 14:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="1CO 14:19" />Ado ke esịd ufọkabasi ami ñkpaakap mma aditañ ikọ ition se inwaña mme awo nọ akpeep mme awo ñkpọ ñkan aditañ ikọ tọsịn duob ke asen edemeikọ.<verse eid="1CO 14:19" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="1CO 14:20" />Nditọeka ke Krais, itre adikere ñkpọ nte ntəkayịn. Akpedo ke usʌñ idiọọkñkpọ ido ntəkayịn, ado ido ñkpoon awo ke akikere ndufo. <verse eid="1CO 14:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="1CO 14:21" />Ke Mbed e-ewet ete:</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="1CO 14:21">“Ami ñyaatañ ikọ nnọ ibon ami</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="1CO 14:21">nto mme awo e-esemme mme usem mfen</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="1CO 14:21">ye ke mme ñkpọkinua isenawo,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="1CO 14:21">ado kpayeado, ammọ idiikpañña utọñ innọ miin,”</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="1CO 14:21">Abọọñ atañ.<verse eid="1CO 14:21" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="1CO 14:22" />Adisem nsio-nsio edemeikọ ado idiọọñọ, ado idooho idiọọñọ inọ mbon e-enịmme Abasi ke akpanikọ, ado idiọọñọ anọ mbon i-imiinịmme Abasi ke akpanikọ. Ado prọfesi ana anọ mbon e-enịmme Abasi ke akpanikọ, inaaha inọ mbon i-imiinịmme Abasi ke akpanikọ. <verse eid="1CO 14:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="1CO 14:23" />Ke ntoro, adieke afịd ufọkabasi ebohoke keed ndin afịd awo esem nsio-nsio edemeikọ, ndin mme mme akoi me mbon i-imiinịmme Abasi ke akpanikọ edʌk edi, nte ammọ idiibooho ke ndufo emedamma? <verse eid="1CO 14:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="1CO 14:24" />Ado adieke awo i-imiinịmme Abasi ke akpanikọ me akoi adʌkkọ adi ke ini afịd awo etañña prọfesi, eyaewọt anye ke anye ado anam idiọọkñkpọ, ñko afịd awo eyaebiom anye ikpe, <verse eid="1CO 14:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="1CO 14:25" />ndin mme ndedịbe ñkpọ esịd ammọ eyaeyaara. Ammọ ndin eyaeduọ ke isọñ ekpono Abasi, enyʌñ ebo, “Ke akpanikọ, Abasi mmọdo ke atu ndufo!”<verse eid="1CO 14:25" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Ukpono Abasi ke Usʌñ A-adotto</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" sid="1CO 14:26" />Nsoo ndin ke ñnyịn idiitañ, nditọeka ke Krais? Ndufo imaidiboho, ndin awo keedekeed anie ikwọ, me ikọ ukpeebñkpọ, me adiyaara, me nsio-nsio edemeikọ me adikappa. Ana enam afịd ñkpọ nọ ato do ufọkabasi akọt. <verse eid="1CO 14:26" /><verse number="27" style="v" sid="1CO 14:27" />Adieke awo asemme asen edemeikọ, yak awo iba, ñwak mbọhọ awo ita esem, awo keedekeed ke ini keed, ndin ana awo akappa se esem. <verse eid="1CO 14:27" /><verse number="28" style="v" sid="1CO 14:28" />Andikappa imiibaaha, yak andisem adop uyio ke ufọkabasi, asem anọ idem amọ ye Abasi.<verse eid="1CO 14:28" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" sid="1CO 14:29" />Yak prọfed iba me ita etañ ikọ, ndin mbon ako ana enekke edomo se etañ. <verse eid="1CO 14:29" /><verse number="30" style="v" sid="1CO 14:30" />Ndin adieke eyaarake ñkpọ enọ awo a-atieghetie, awo andikito ntañ ikọ ana atre. <verse eid="1CO 14:30" /><verse number="31" style="v" sid="1CO 14:31" />Sia afịd ndufo eyaekan etañ prọfesi ke adiana ke adiana, nọ afịd awo ekan ebọ ukpeeb enyʌñ enie nsọọñọnda. <verse eid="1CO 14:31" /><verse number="32" style="v" sid="1CO 14:32" />Mme sịbidịd mme prọfed eba ke nsuukiwuod enọ mme prọfed. <verse eid="1CO 14:32" /><verse number="33" style="v" sid="1CO 14:33" />Sia Abasi idooho Abasi ndutịme ado ado Abasi emem, kpa naña ado ke afịd mbono ikọd Abasi.<verse eid="1CO 14:33" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="34" style="v" sid="1CO 14:34" />Ibaan ikpinaaha esio uyio ke esịd ufọkabasi. Inaaha ammọ etañ ikọ, ado ana eba ke idak nsuukiwuod, kpa naña mbed atañ. <verse eid="1CO 14:34" /><verse number="35" style="v" sid="1CO 14:35" />Adieke ammọ enieghe mbuume ebaña ñkpọ akeedodo, yak ammọ ebịp mme ebe ammọ ke ufọk; sia ado ñkpọ abuud awonwaan aditañ ikọ ke esịd ufọkabasi.<verse eid="1CO 14:35" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="36" style="v" sid="1CO 14:36" />Nte ikọ Abasi akito ndufo asakka? Me ado nte ndufo ikpọọñ ke ikọ Abasi akesịm? <verse eid="1CO 14:36" /><verse number="37" style="v" sid="1CO 14:37" />Adieke awo akeeadodo akereke ke mmimọ ido prọfed me iminie enọ sịbidịd, yak ammọ enyịmme ke se ami ñwet ami ado ewʌhọ Abasi. <verse eid="1CO 14:37" /><verse number="38" style="v" sid="1CO 14:38" />Adieke awo ndomokeed asịnne ikọ ami, eyaenyʌñ esịn ammọ.<verse eid="1CO 14:38" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="39" style="v" sid="1CO 14:39" />Ke ntoro, nditọeka mmi ke Krais, inie udọñ aditañ prọfesi, ikiinyʌñ ikpan adisem nsio-nsio edemeikọ. <verse eid="1CO 14:39" /><verse number="40" style="v" sid="1CO 14:40" />Ado yak enam afịd ñkpọ ke usʌñ a-adotto.<verse eid="1CO 14:40" /></para>
  <chapter eid="1CO 14" />
  <chapter number="15" style="c" sid="1CO 15" />
  <para style="s1">Adised Krais</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="1CO 15:1" />Nditọeka ke Krais, ami ñyem aditoiyo ndufo eti etob a-ami ñkekwọrọ inọọ ndufo, a-ndufo ekebọọhọ, e-ekenyʌññọ enie nsọọñọnda. <verse eid="1CO 15:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="1CO 15:2" />Ato ke eti etob ami ndufo ebọ adinyaaña, adieke ndufo esọọñọke eda ke se ami ñkekwọrọ inọọ ndufo. Imiidooho ntoro, adinịm ke akpanikọ ndufo ado ikpu-ikpu.<verse eid="1CO 15:2" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="1CO 15:3" />Sia se ami ñkebọọ ke ñkekpọñ inọọ ndufo nte ataa akpan ñkpọ: Ke Krais amaakpa ke ntak idiọọkñkpọ ñnyịn, kpa naña ewet ke ñwed Abasi, <verse eid="1CO 15:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="1CO 15:4" />ke emaebuuk anye, ndin emaenam anye aset ke ayọhọ usen ita kpa naña ewet ke ñwed Abasi, <verse eid="1CO 15:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="1CO 15:5" />ndin ke anye amaayaara idem awọt Kefas<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">15:5 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Kefas ado Pita</char></note> ye mme mbed duob mme iba. <verse eid="1CO 15:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="1CO 15:6" />Ke ado aboiyoke, anye amaayaara idem awọt mme nditọeka ke Krais e-ekewakka ekan awo ikie ition, uwak ammọ mmọdo ke uwem, akpesʌkado usʌk emaedaiya. <verse eid="1CO 15:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="1CO 15:7" />Akema anye amaayaara idem awọt Yems, ndin afịd mme abọsịd, <verse eid="1CO 15:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="1CO 15:8" />ndin ke akpatre anye amaayaara idem añwọt miin ñko, nte anye a-akemanake ke atikwo-atikwo usʌñ.<verse eid="1CO 15:8" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="1CO 15:9" />Sia ami ndo andisịp ñkan ke atu mme abọsịd, ndotto se ekpekoot abọsịd sia mmaakọbọ ufọk Abasi. <verse eid="1CO 15:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="1CO 15:10" />Ado ato ke mfọn Abasi, ami ndo se ami ndo, ndin mfọn amọ ikidooho ke utak-utak. Iyoo, mmaanam utom ñkan afịd mme abọsịd mbon ñko, idooho ke ukeme mmi, ado ato ke mfọn Abasi a-akebaaha ye ami. <verse eid="1CO 15:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="1CO 15:11" />Idahami, me ato ke ami-o, me ato ke ammọ-o, se ñnyịn ikwọrọ ado ami, ñko se ndufo ekenyʌñ enịm ado ado.<verse eid="1CO 15:11" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Adised mme Akpañkpa</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="1CO 15:12" />Ado adieke ekwọrọke ebo ke emaenam Krais aset ke ñkpa, usʌk ndufo enam die ebo ke adised ke ñkpa ibaaha? <verse eid="1CO 15:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="1CO 15:13" />Adieke adised ke ñkpa imiibaaha, awuọñọ ke Krais ke idem amọ ikiisette. <verse eid="1CO 15:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="1CO 15:14" />Ndin adieke Krais imiikisette, awuọñọ ke ukwọrọikọ ñnyịn ye mbuọdidem ndufo ado ikpu-ikpu. <verse eid="1CO 15:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="1CO 15:15" />Ke akanna ado, mme awo ediikịt ñnyịn nte idoñño mme ntiense nsu ibaña Abasi, sia ñnyịn imitie ntiense ibaña Abasi ibo ke anye akenam Krais aset ke ñkpa. Ado Abasi ikinamma Krais aset, adieke ke akpanikọ mme akpañkpa imiisette. <verse eid="1CO 15:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="1CO 15:16" />Sia adieke imiikpinamma mme akpañkpa eset, awuọ ke awo ikinyʌññọ inam Krais aset. <verse eid="1CO 15:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="1CO 15:17" />Ndin adieke Krais imiikisette, mbuọdidem ndufo ado ikpu-ikpu; esʌk enyeenyịne ke idiọọkñkpọ ndufo. <verse eid="1CO 15:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="1CO 15:18" />Ndin mbon e-ekekpaññake ke Krais e-etak. <verse eid="1CO 15:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="1CO 15:19" />Adieke ñnyịn inieghe idodanyen ke Krais ke uwem ami ikpọọñ, awuọñọ mbọm ñnyịn a-akpon eti-eti akan afịd mbon mfen.<verse eid="1CO 15:19" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="1CO 15:20" />Ado ke akpanikọ emaenam Krais aset ke ñkpa, akpa mbunwịm mbon e-ekpaññake. <verse eid="1CO 15:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="1CO 15:21" />Sia ñkpa aketooho awo keed adi, adised ke ñkpa anyʌñ ato awo keed adi. <verse eid="1CO 15:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="1CO 15:22" />Sia atooho ke Adam afịd awo ekpa, ñko ke Krais eyaenam afịd awo edu uwem. <verse eid="1CO 15:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="1CO 15:23" />Ado anie ini amọ anie: Krais, akpa mbunwịm, ndin anye amaadi, mbon se ido ake amọ ediana. <verse eid="1CO 15:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="1CO 15:24" />Ndin utịd ayaadi, ini se Krais adiikpọñ abioubọọñ inọ Abasi Ete ke ini anye amaakesobo afịd adudu ye ukara. <verse eid="1CO 15:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="1CO 15:25" />Sia ana anye akara tutu anye asịn mme asua amọ ke idak ñkpad amọ. <verse eid="1CO 15:25" /><verse number="26" style="v" sid="1CO 15:26" />Akpatre asua e-ediisobo ado ñkpa. <verse eid="1CO 15:26" /><verse number="27" style="v" sid="1CO 15:27" />Sia anye, “asịn afịd ñkpọ ke idak ñkpad amọ.” Ndin emaebo, “afịd ñkpọ” asịne ke idak amọ, e-ediọọñọ ke Abasi ke idem amọ isịneke ke idak ado, sia anye ado andikisịn afịd ñkpọ ke idak Krais. <verse eid="1CO 15:27" /><verse number="28" style="v" sid="1CO 15:28" />Ke ini anye amaakenam ami, Ayịn ayaasuuk iwuod anọ andikisịn afịd ñkpọ ke idak amọ, nọ Abasi ado afịd ke afịd.<verse eid="1CO 15:28" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" sid="1CO 15:29" />Ndin adieke adised ke ñkpa imiibaaha, mbon e-eduọkkọ mmọọñ enọ mme akpañkpa ediinam die? Adieke mme akpañkpa imiidiisette, ntak a-ambon awo eduọkkọ mmọọñ enọ ammọ-ọ? <verse eid="1CO 15:29" /><verse number="30" style="v" sid="1CO 15:30" />Ndin ñnyịn ntom, ntak a-ñnyịn isioho idem ñnyịn inyan anwa-anwa-a? <verse eid="1CO 15:30" /><verse number="31" style="v" sid="1CO 15:31" />Kwa usen ami ñkịt ñkpa ke anyen, akpanikọ ke ntañ, kpa naña nduaak inua ke ntak ndufo ke Krais Yisọs Abọọñ ñnyịn. <verse eid="1CO 15:31" /><verse number="32" style="v" sid="1CO 15:32" />Adieke ami ñkekamake idodanyen ikpọkidem kpọd ñnwana ye mme afai unam ke Efisọs, nsoo ido udod mmi? Adieke mme akpañkpa imiisette,</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="1CO 15:32">“Yak ñnyịn idia inyʌñ inwọñ,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="1CO 15:32">sia ñkpọñ ñnyịn iyaikpañña.”<verse eid="1CO 15:32" /></para>
  <para style="m">
    <verse number="33" style="v" sid="1CO 15:33" />Ikiiyak awo itịn ndufo usʌñ: “Idiọọk nsaña ababiat eti edu.”<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">15:33 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Ikọ ami ado ikọ Menanda, awet uto awo Greek</char></note> <verse eid="1CO 15:33" /><verse number="34" style="v" sid="1CO 15:34" />Itịmme idinie nti iwuod ndufo naña ekpeba, inyʌñ itre edinam idiọọkñkpọ; sia a-aba mbon i-imiinieghe ifiọk ibaña Abasi; ami ntañ ami nọ abuud imʌm ndufo.<verse eid="1CO 15:34" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Adised Ikpọkidem</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="35" style="v" sid="1CO 15:35" />Ado awo ayaabịp, “Mme akpañkpa enam die eset? Nsoo utọ ikpọkidem ke ammọ ediinie?” <verse eid="1CO 15:35" /><verse number="36" style="v" sid="1CO 15:36" />Ataa ndisịme! Se awo atọ ikemeke aditịppe ibọhọke ñkpọ ado akpa. <verse eid="1CO 15:36" /><verse number="37" style="v" sid="1CO 15:37" />Awo amaatọ ñkpọ, idooho se anye adiidọk ke anye atọ, ñkpasi kpọd ke etọ, me ake abakpa me ñkpọ mfen. <verse eid="1CO 15:37" /><verse number="38" style="v" sid="1CO 15:38" />Ado Abasi anọ anye idem naña anye abiide, ndin anye anọ nsio-nsio ñkpasi asaña-asaña idem. <verse eid="1CO 15:38" /><verse number="39" style="v" sid="1CO 15:39" />Afịd ikpọkidem idooho ukem: Awo anie utọ idem keed, unam anie mfen, inuen utọ mfen, iyak utọ mfen. <verse eid="1CO 15:39" /><verse number="40" style="v" sid="1CO 15:40" />Idem ake hefịn mmọdo, idem ake isọñ mmọdo ñko; ado uyai idem ake hefịn ado isio-isio, idem ake isọñ anyʌñ ado isio-isio. <verse eid="1CO 15:40" /><verse number="41" style="v" sid="1CO 15:41" />Utịn a-anie asaña-asaña uyai amọ, afiọñ ñko a-anie asaña-asaña uyai amọ ye mme ntantaafiọñ ñko; ntantaafiọñ keed akpəho ye ntantaafiọñ mfen ke uyai.<verse eid="1CO 15:41" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="42" style="v" sid="1CO 15:42" />Ukem ami ke adiido ke adised mme akpañkpa. Idem e-etọọhọ ado mbiara, ado amaaset ibiarake; <verse eid="1CO 15:42" /><verse number="43" style="v" sid="1CO 15:43" />etọ ke asuenne, adiset ke ubọọñ; etọ ke mmemidem, adiset ke adudu; <verse eid="1CO 15:43" /><verse number="44" style="v" sid="1CO 15:44" />etọ ke abʌkidem, adiset ke idem sịbidịd.</para>
  <para style="p" vid="1CO 15:44">Adieke abʌkidem abaaha, ana idem sịbidịd ñko anyʌñ aba. <verse eid="1CO 15:44" /><verse number="45" style="v" sid="1CO 15:45" />Ke ntoro e-ewet: “Akpa awo Adam ado aduuwem ñkpọ,” akpatre Adam, ado anọ uwem sịbidịd. <verse eid="1CO 15:45" /><verse number="46" style="v" sid="1CO 15:46" />Idooho sịbidịd aketo adi, ado abʌkidem, ke ado aboiyoke sịbidịd adiana. <verse eid="1CO 15:46" /><verse number="47" style="v" sid="1CO 15:47" />Akpa awo akedo ntọñ isọñ, ayọhọ awo iba ato hefịn. <verse eid="1CO 15:47" /><verse number="48" style="v" sid="1CO 15:48" />Kpa naña awo ederimbod akeba, kpa ntoro ke mbon e-etooho ntan isọñ ebañña; naña awo hefịn aba, ntoro ñko ke mbon hefịn ebañña. <verse eid="1CO 15:48" /><verse number="49" style="v" sid="1CO 15:49" />Kpa naña ñnyịn inie mbid awo a-atooho ntan isọñ, ntoro ñko ke idiinie mbid awo a-atooho hefịn.<verse eid="1CO 15:49" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="50" style="v" sid="1CO 15:50" />Ntañ inọ ndufo, nditọeka ke Krais, nte ke abʌk ye iyiib ikanna adinie udeeme ke abioubọọñ Abasi, me mbiara adinie udeeme ke se imiibiarake. <verse eid="1CO 15:50" /><verse number="51" style="v" sid="1CO 15:51" />Ikpañ utọñ, ami idọkkọ ndufo ndịbe-ndịbe ñkpọ. Idooho afịd ñnyịn idiikpa, ado eyaenam afịd ñnyịn ikpəho <verse eid="1CO 15:51" /><verse number="52" style="v" sid="1CO 15:52" />ke adibọp anyen ntat, ke akpatre adukpoñ amaasio uyio. Sia adukpoñ ayaasio uyio, ndin eyaenam mme akpañkpa eset ye ikpọkidem i-imiidiibiarake ndin eyaikpəho ñnyịn. <verse eid="1CO 15:52" /><verse number="53" style="v" sid="1CO 15:53" />Sia se ido mbiara ana akappa ado se imiidibiarake, ndin ikpaikpa ñkpọ akappa anie nsi-nsi uwem. <verse eid="1CO 15:53" /><verse number="54" style="v" sid="1CO 15:54" />Ke ini mbiara amaakappa ado se imiibiarake, ikpaikpa ñko akappa anie uwem, ndin se ekewet ayaadisu: “Adikan a-aben ñkpa amen.”<verse eid="1CO 15:54" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="55" style="v" sid="1CO 15:55" />“O ñkpa, mmọ adikan mfo?</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="1CO 15:55">O ñkpa, mmọ ifod mfo?”<verse eid="1CO 15:55" /></para>
  <para style="m">
    <verse number="56" style="v" sid="1CO 15:56" />Ifod ñkpa ado idiọọkñkpọ, adudu ñkpa ado mbed. <verse eid="1CO 15:56" /><verse number="57" style="v" sid="1CO 15:57" />Ado ekọọm anie Abasi! Anye i-inọ ñnyịn adikan ato Abọọñ ñnyịn Yisọs Krais.<verse eid="1CO 15:57" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="58" style="v" sid="1CO 15:58" />Ke ntoro, ndima nditọeka mmi ke Krais, isọọñọ ida. Ikiiyak ñkpọ ndomokeed inyeeñe ndufo. Isịn idem ndufo ayọhọ-ayọhọ afid ini ke utom Abọọñ, sia emediọọñọ ke ñwaidem ndufo idooho utak-utak.<verse eid="1CO 15:58" /></para>
  <chapter eid="1CO 15" />
  <chapter number="16" style="c" sid="1CO 16" />
  <para style="s1">Etịbe A-anieghe Ikọd Abasi</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="1CO 16:1" />Ndin ke abaña etịbe a-anieghe ikọd Abasi, inam se ñkebo mme ikọd Abasi ke mme ufọkabasi Kalesia enam. <verse eid="1CO 16:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="1CO 16:2" />Ke akpa usen ke afịd udua, awo keedekeed akpena adiañña asaña-asaña akʌk anịm akeene se anye anie, abọọk anịm, nọ ado ami mmaadi, etịbe idiibaaha aba. <verse eid="1CO 16:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="1CO 16:3" />Ndin, ami mmaadisịm, ñyaanọ mme awo se ndufo emek ñnyʌñ nnọ ammọ ñwed adiben ammọ ñwọt ye enọ ndufo nọ eben eka Yeruselem. <verse eid="1CO 16:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="1CO 16:4" />Adieke anaaha nte ami ñkeene ñka, ammọ eyaeñkeene miin.<verse eid="1CO 16:4" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Mme Akpọ-akpọ Ebeeñe Mmi</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="1CO 16:5" />Ami mmaaboiyo nto Masidonia ndi, ami ñyaadise ndufo, sia ndiisaña mboiyo ke Masidonia. <verse eid="1CO 16:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="1CO 16:6" />Akeme ido ami ñyaaba etək ye ndufo, akeme ido ñyaaba do afịd ini ekarika, nọ ndufo esịn unwam ennọ ke isañ mmi, ke itie akeedodo a-ami ñyemme adika. <verse eid="1CO 16:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="1CO 16:7" />Ami ñyemme adidi usọp-usọp ñnyʌñ mboiyo; mmeyem adikpiba ñkpeene ye ndufo, ke Abasi anyịmmeke. <verse eid="1CO 16:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="1CO 16:8" />Ado ami ñyaaba ke Efisọs tutu akem ini Pentikọs, <verse eid="1CO 16:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="1CO 16:9" />sia ekamba usʌñ adinam eti utom a-abeere annọ, uwak awo ñko mmọdo e-ebeeñeke idem edimbiọñọ miin.<verse eid="1CO 16:9" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="1CO 16:10" />Timoti akpedi, ikịt ibo ke anye inieghe ntak adikop ndịk ke ini anye abaaha ye ndufo, sia anye anam utom Abasi, kpa naña ami nnam. <verse eid="1CO 16:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="1CO 16:11" />Ke awo ndomokeed asọọn anye. Isio anye unyọñ ke emem nọ anye atịmme ambịne miin. Nsʌk mbet anye ye mme nditọeka ke Krais mbon ako.<verse eid="1CO 16:11" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="1CO 16:12" />Ndin ke abaña ayịneka ñnyịn Apọlọs, mmaanekke mbo yak anye ye nditọeka ke Krais edibịne ndufo. Anye ikinyịmmeke adika idahami, ado ayaakaa ufañ amaamaana aba.<verse eid="1CO 16:12" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="1CO 16:13" />Iba ke ñkpemeidem, isọọñọ ida ke mbuọdidem, ido mbon uko; isọñ idem. <verse eid="1CO 16:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="1CO 16:14" />Inam afịd ñkpọ ke ima.<verse eid="1CO 16:14" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="1CO 16:15" />Ndufo emediọọñọ ke ufọk Stefanas ekedo mme akpa mbon e-ekekappake esịd ke Akaya, ndin ammọ emaewa idem asaña-asaña ke adinwam mme ikọd Abasi. Mmikpeiye ndufo nditọeka ke Krais nte <verse eid="1CO 16:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="1CO 16:16" />esuuk iwuod enọ utọ ibon ami ye afịd awo se idian ubọk inam utom inyʌñ iwa idem. <verse eid="1CO 16:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="1CO 16:17" />Mmaakop inemesịd ke ini Stefanas, Fọtunatus ye Akaikus ekedisịmme, sia ammọ emaeben se ikinana ñnyịn eto ndufo edi. <verse eid="1CO 16:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="1CO 16:18" />Ammọ emaedemme sịbidịd mmi ye ake ndufo ñko. Utọ ibon ami edot ukpono.<verse eid="1CO 16:18" /></para>
  <para style="b" />
  <para style="s1">Akpatre Ekọọm</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="1CO 16:19" />Mme ufọkabasi ke ikpeghe Esia enọ ekọọm isọk ndufo.</para>
  <para style="p" vid="1CO 16:19">Akwila ye Prisila<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">16:19 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Ke usem Greek </char><char style="fqa" closed="false">Priska</char><char style="ft" closed="false">asʌk ado </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Prisila</char></note> e-enekke ikọọm ndufo ke Abọọñ, ukem ñko ye ufọkabasi a-asisooboke ke ufọk ammọ.<verse eid="1CO 16:19" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="1CO 16:20" />Afịd nditọeka ideen ye ibaan ke Krais ke ukañ umi e-enọ ekọọm isọk ndufo.</para>
  <para style="p" vid="1CO 16:20">Ikọọm emọ-emọ ye adisana ntʌminua.<verse eid="1CO 16:20" /></para>
  <para style="b" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="1CO 16:21" />Ami Pọọl, ñwet ekọọm ami ke ubọk mmi.<verse eid="1CO 16:21" /></para>
  <para style="b" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="1CO 16:22" />Adieke awo ndomokeed imiimaaha Abọọñ, yak esuuñọ utọ awo ado! Di, Abọọñ!<verse eid="1CO 16:22" /></para>
  <para style="b" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" sid="1CO 16:23" />Mfọn Abọọñ Yisọs Krais akpekam aba ye ndufo.<verse eid="1CO 16:23" /></para>
  <para style="b" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" sid="1CO 16:24" />Yak ima mmi aba ye afịd ndufo ke Krais Yisọs, Amen<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">16:24 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Usʌk mme ikpañwed isịnne </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Amen</char></note>.<verse eid="1CO 16:24" /></para>
  <chapter eid="1CO 16" />
</usx>